UPDATE companies SET description='Rocky Mountain Circuits operates from Longmont, Colorado, where it has fabricated printed circuit boards since 1972.

The shop produces double-sided through 24-layer multilayer boards, including rigid, flex, and rigid-flex constructions. Processes cover blind and buried vias, filled vias, sequential lamination, microvias, controlled-depth milling, backdrilling, and impedance modeling with 3-mil line/space capability. Surface finishes include HASL (lead-free and standard), ENIG, and immersion silver. Materials range from standard FR4 to high-frequency Rogers, Taconic, Nelco, and Teflon substrates, plus aluminum-based boards for thermal management. The facility also assembles custom cable harnesses and provides box-build integration, offering a prototype-to-production flow with quick-turn options as fast as 48 hours and standard leads of 10 days. Offshore partners handle higher-volume runs.

Customers span medical devices, industrial automation, automotive electronics, consumer products, semiconductor test, Internet of Things, energy systems, and network/telecommunications infrastructure. The company cites work in each of these sectors on its website.

Rocky Mountain Circuits attributes its longevity to a philosophy of building high-quality product, delivering on time, and pricing competitively. It emphasizes rapid turnaround, UL-approved material compliance, and a one-stop model that includes fabrication, assembly, cable, and box-build services.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Double-sided PCB fabrication", "Multilayer PCB fabrication (up to 24 layers)", "Rigid-flex and flex PCB fabrication", "RF antenna fabrication", "Blind vias", "Buried vias", "Filled vias", "Sequential lamination", "Microvias", "Impedance modeling and testing", "3 mil line/space resolution", "Controlled depth milling", "Backdrilling", "HASL (lead-free and standard)", "ENIG", "Immersion silver", "Custom cable assemblies", "Box build integration", "Design services", "Exotic IoT and RF designs", "TDR modeling and testing", "Quick-turn prototypes (24-hour to 7-day)", "Standard production lead time (10 days)", "Offshore high-volume production sourcing"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Industrial Automation", "Automotive Electronics", "Consumer Electronics", "Semiconductor", "Internet of Things", "Energy Applications", "Network & Telecommunication"], "materials": ["FR4", "Rogers", "Taconic", "Polyimide", "Aluminum", "Duroid/Ceramic", "Teflon RF Substrates", "Nelco"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "As fast as 48 hours for quick-turn; standard 10 days", "tolerances": "3 mil lines and spaces", "built_on": ["48-hour quick-turn prototype service", "UL-approved FR4 and Canadian UL material compliance", "Aluminum substrates for high-heat LED designs", "RF antennas on Rogers, Taconic, and Nelco laminates", "One-stop prototype-to-production including cable assemblies and box builds"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db", "Headquarters Longmont, Colorado -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "ITAR registered -> /", "Quick-turn as fast as 48 hours -> /", "Up to 24 layers -> /", "Materials: FR4, Rogers, Taconic, Polyimide, Aluminum -> /", "Industries: Medical Devices, Industrial, Automobile, Consumer Electronics, Semiconductor, IoT, Energy Applications, Network & Telecommunication -> /", "Capabilities: blind/buried vias, filled vias, sequential lamination, microvias, impedance modeling, 3/3 lines/spaces, controlled depth milling, backdrilling, ENIG, immersion silver, HASL, flex/rigid-flex, custom cable assemblies, box builds -> /services", "RF antennas on Rogers/Taconic/Nelco -> /", "Offshore sourcing for high volume -> /", "UL approved FR4 -> /", "Canadian UL -> /", "Lead times: 24 hour to 7-day quickturns, 10-day standard -> /services", "Prototype to production -> /services", "One-stop solution -> /", "Company philosophy: build high-quality product, deliver on-time, competitive price -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Rockymountain Circuits has been providing high quality printed circuit boards to the electronics industry since 1972.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rocky-mountain-circuits' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='S&K Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1984 by the Confederated Salish and Kootenai Tribes on the Flathead Indian Reservation in Ronan, Montana. The tribally-owned company operates from a 42,000-square-foot facility spanning three buildings in the Mission Valley.

The contract manufacturer specializes in high-reliability circuit card assembly using surface-mount and through-hole technologies, custom wire harnesses, and electromechanical box builds. Its capabilities extend to automated optical inspection, flying probe and in-circuit testing, 2D/3D X-ray inspection, conformal coating, and an in-house precision machine shop. The facility supports high-mix, low-to-high volume turnkey production with a workforce of 51 to 200 employees.

The company is ITAR registered and holds AS9100D certification, making it a qualified supplier for mission-critical defense and aerospace programs.

S&K emphasizes financially stable operations, 100% inspection and testing, and adherence to IPC Class 3 workmanship standards as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015 Compliant','AS9100D Aerospace Certified','ITAR Registered','IPC-A-610 Class 3 Certified','IPC/WHMA-A-620 Class 3 Certified','IPC J-STD-001 Certified Trainers & Operators','HUBZone Certified Small Disadvantaged Business','GIDEP Member','ERAI Member']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole PCB Assembly & Mixed Technology", "Custom Cable & Wire Harness Assembly", "Electromechanical Box Build & System Integration", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Flying Probe & Functional In-Circuit Testing", "2D / 3D X-Ray Inspection", "Conformal Coating & Potting Services", "In-House Precision Machine Shop & Tooling", "Engineering & DFM Design Support (Altium, NI LabVIEW, SolidWorks)", "High-Mix / Low-to-High Volume Turnkey Production"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense / Military", "Industrial Automation & Controls", "Medical Equipment", "Telecommunications & Networking", "Energy & Power Systems", "Commercial OEM Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Flying Probe & Functional In-Circuit Testing", "2D / 3D X-Ray Inspection", "Selective Wave Soldering"], "volume": "Low-to-high volume turnkey production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tribally-owned by the Confederated Salish and Kootenai Tribes", "HUBZone certified small disadvantaged business", "ITAR registered with AS9100D certification", "In-house precision machine shop and engineering support", "42,000-square-foot facility with advanced inspection and test equipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 by Confederated Salish and Kootenai Tribes -> db", "Tribally-owned, Native American-owned -> /about-us", "Headquarters Ronan, Montana on Flathead Indian Reservation -> db, /about-us", "42,000-square-foot facility across three buildings -> db, /about-us", "Employee count 51-200 -> db", "Capabilities: SMT, through-hole, wire harness, box build, AOI, flying probe, X-ray, conformal coating, machine shop, engineering support, turnkey production -> db", "Industries served: aerospace/defense, industrial, medical, telecom, energy, commercial OEM -> db", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ITAR, IPC-A-610 Class 3, IPC/WHMA-A-620 Class 3, IPC J-STD-001, HUBZone, GIDEP, ERAI -> db, /about-us", "CAGE code 6Y268 -> /about-us", "Volume: high-mix low-to-high volume turnkey -> db", "Differentiators: tribal ownership, HUBZone, ITAR, AS9100, in-house machine shop, 100% inspection -> /about-us, db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "electronics contract manufacturer", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "51-200", "cage_code": "6Y268", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["HUBZone", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='s-k-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SHINE Wire was founded in 1984 in Adams, Massachusetts. The company operates from a manufacturing center and specializes in cable assemblies, wire harnesses, and electro-mechanical assemblies.

Its core services include custom cable assembly, wire harnessing, electro-mechanical assembly (box build), lead wire assembly, cordsets, wire and cable processing, engineering support for new product introduction and design for manufacturing, and testing for performance, safety, and compliance. The shop performs certified soldering and crimping, crimp height verification, crimp pull testing, hipot testing, and computerized testing, supported by tooling calibration, machine maintenance, and statistical process control reporting.

SHINE serves medical device manufacturers such as Smith Medical, along with other electronics and industrial customers requiring UL/CSA-compliant cordsets and RoHS-compliant assemblies. The company holds a UL Recognized Registration (E111307) and CSA recognition, and its products meet IPC/WHMA-A-620 standards.

The company emphasizes a blend of engineering resources, account management, and a vetted global supply chain, positioning itself as a quality-driven contract manufacturer. SHINE is a member of the Wire Harness Manufacturers Association and contributed to the development of the IPC-620 standard, reflecting its commitment to industry standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC/WHMA-A-620','UL Recognized Registration #E111307','CSA','RoHS','ANAB accredited']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Wire harnessing", "Electro-mechanical assembly (box build)", "Lead wire assembly", "Cordsets (UL/CSA standards)", "Wire and cable processing (cut/strip)", "Engineering support (NPI, DFM)", "Testing (performance, safety, reliability, compliance)", "Certified soldering", "Certified crimping", "Crimp height verification", "Crimp pull testing", "Hipot testing", "Computerized testing", "Tooling calibration", "Machine maintenance", "SPC reporting", "First article inspection", "In-process inspection", "Final inspection"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified with TUV Rhineland of North America", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 certified", "UL Recognized (E111307) and CSA recognized", "RoHS compliant", "WHMA member and contributor to IPC-620 standard"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 -> db", "Headquarters Adams, Massachusetts -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with TUV Rhineland -> /quality", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 certified -> /quality", "UL Recognized Registration #E111307 -> /quality", "CSA recognized -> /quality", "RoHS compliant -> /quality", "ANAB accredited -> /quality", "Services: custom cable assembly, wire harnessing, electro-mechanical assembly, lead wire assembly, cordsets, wire and cable processing, engineering support, testing -> /services", "Certified soldering and crimping, crimp height verification, crimp pull testing, hipot testing, computerized testing, tooling calibration, machine maintenance, weekly training, SPC reports, customer meetings -> /quality", "WHMA member and contributor to IPC-620 standard -> /quality", "Testimonial from Smith Medical -> /quality", "Company described as electronic contract manufacturer -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SHINE is a quality-driven electronic contract manufacturer", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='shine-wire' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SMC Integration Solutions, LLC was founded in 1996 in Nicholasville, Kentucky.

The company provides electronic manufacturing services (EMS) and systems integration, including printed circuit board assembly, custom cable and wire harness assembly, complex box build, and full assembly testing. Its capabilities span new product introduction (NPI) and rapid prototyping through low-, medium-, and high-volume production. SMC maintains five dedicated engineering groups—customer, test, process, quality, and systems integration—supported by a strategic business management function. The operations team comprises engineers and professionals with 30-plus years of experience assembling high-technology products.

SMC serves the medical device, aerospace and defense, industrial controls, security, military/DOD, construction, and transportation industries. Medical customers include manufacturers of MRI, PET, and CT imaging equipment as well as biomedical freezers. The company is ISO 13485:2016 registered for medical devices, ISO 9001:2015 registered, FDA registered, and manufactures to IPC-A-610 Rev G standards. A recent blog post notes a contract manufacturing agreement with COMSovereign for radio production.

SMC emphasizes a partnership model built on its “4 P’s”—Principles, People, Process, and Performance—and offers direct fulfillment to end customers. Differentiators cited by the company include an electronic 8D corrective-action system integrated with its ERP, a manufacturing execution system tailored for EMS, and in-house development of test systems to ensure product reliability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','FDA Registered (Registration Number 3009627223)','IPC-A-610 Rev G','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design support services", "New product introduction (NPI) & prototyping", "PCB assembly (including complex PCBA, low/medium/high volume)", "ICT and functional test", "RF experience", "Systems integration (sub-assembly, complex box build, full assembly testing)", "Custom product configuration", "Product certification support (CE, CSA, SGS, UL)", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Wire harness and cable assembly", "Focused engineering support (test engineering, customer engineering, quality engineering, SMT process engineering, systems integration)", "Transition management (initial inventory management, quote/forecast management, project management)", "Strategic business management (project management, strategic planning, tactical planning)", "Supply chain & materials management (supply chain relationships, professional inventory management, sourcing)", "Direct fulfillment & logistics solutions (returnable packaging, customer warehousing, direct fulfillment)", "Design review (analysis for manufacturability, testability, procurement)", "Rapid prototype", "Pre-production build", "Product configuration (implement configure order system)"], "industries": ["Medical device", "Aerospace & defense", "Industrial controls", "Security", "Military/DOD", "Construction", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Five dedicated engineering groups (customer, test, process, quality, systems integration) plus strategic business management", "Direct fulfillment and logistics solutions including returnable packaging and customer warehousing", "Electronic 8D corrective-action system fully integrated with ERP", "Manufacturing execution system tailored for EMS with interlocking process tracking", "Two Kentucky locations providing regional access for technology customers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Nicholasville, Kentucky -> db", "ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, FDA Registered, IPC-A-610 Rev G, RoHS certifications -> / (home page) and /quality", "Two Kentucky locations -> /quality", "Five dedicated engineering groups -> / (home page) and /services", "Strategic Business Management role -> / (home page) and /services", "Direct fulfillment and logistics solutions -> / (home page) and /services", "Electronic 8D corrective action system integrated with ERP -> /quality", "Manufacturing Execution System tailored for EMS -> /quality", "Industries served: medical, aerospace & defense, industrial controls, security, military/DOD, construction, transportation -> / (home page) and /quality", "Medical imaging equipment (MRI, PET, CT) and biomedical freezers -> / (home page)", "COMSovereign contract manufacturing agreement -> /quality (blog post)", "PCB assembly, cable assembly, box build, NPI, prototyping, design support, test engineering -> /capabilities and / (home page)", "L-M-H volume production -> /capabilities", "Product certification support (CE, CSA, SGS, UL) -> /capabilities", "Wire harness and cable assembly -> /capabilities", "30+ years experience of operations team -> / (home page) and /capabilities", "Principles, People, Process, Performance (4 P''s) -> / (home page)", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SMC is a print circuit board assembly manufacturer, custom cable assembly provider, system integration/box build manufacturer", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/3082160/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='smc-integration-solutions-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SMK Packaging was founded in 2011 by Steven Karlsrud in Reno, Nevada.

The company controls the full production chain in‑house: blown film extrusion using three‑layer coextrusion and six‑component gravimetric dosing, prepress services including design, trapping, bar coding and plate making, printing on two eight‑color central impression flexographic presses capable of 50‑inch web width, and converting that produces wicketed bags, side‑weld bags, roll stock with vent holes, zippers and handle features. An on‑site laboratory performs OTR, tensile, dart, seal strength, haze, gloss, density and melt‑flow testing on resins, films and finished goods.

SMK primarily serves fresh‑produce packers and other food‑contact packaging customers across the western U.S., and is expanding into additional markets that require short lead times and responsive service. Its packaging is designed for vertical and horizontal form‑fill‑seal equipment used in automated and hand‑pack lines.

The business was built on a vision of responsiveness and vertical integration, aiming to eliminate bottlenecks by keeping every step under one roof. Management emphasizes flexibility — offering rush orders and custom film structures without long queue times — and maintains GMP and HACCP programs audited by third parties to ensure safety for direct food contact.', certifications=ARRAY['GMP','HACCP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown film extrusion (three-layer coextrusion)", "Gravimetric dosing (six-component)", "Prepress (design, trapping, bar coding, color separation, plate making)", "Flexographic printing (8-color central impression)", "Converting (slitting, wicketed bags, side-weld bags, vent holes, PTC zippers, handle holes, flips)", "Laboratory testing (OTR, tensile, dart, seal strength, haze, gloss, density, melt flow)"], "industries": ["Fresh produce", "Food packaging"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Two eight-color central impression flexographic printing presses (50\" web width, 26\" repeat)", "Blown film extrusion line with three-layer (A/B/C) coextrusion and six-component automated gravimetric dosing", "In-house laboratory equipment for OTR, tensile, dart, seal strength, haze, gloss, density, melt flow"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated production from extrusion through converting and lab testing", "In\u2011house prepress and plate making for faster turnaround", "Two eight\u2011color central impression flexo presses (50\" web width)", "GMP and HACCP certified for direct food contact packaging"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2011 by Steven Karlsrud -> /", "Headquarters in Reno, Nevada -> db", "Vertically integrated flexible packaging manufacturer -> /", "Processes: extrusion, prepress, printing, converting, laboratory -> /", "Certifications: GMP, HACCP -> /", "Focus on fresh produce market in western USA -> /", "Two high-speed eight-color CI flexo presses (50\" web width) -> /", "In-house laboratory testing capabilities (OTR, tensile, dart, seal strength, haze, gloss, density, melt flow) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SMK Packaging is a vertically integrated low cost manufacturer of high quality custom-made flexible packaging", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='smk-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company remains independently owned, with ownership actively involved in daily operations alongside experienced department heads. It began as a clam harvesting and processing venture and has grown into a vertically integrated seafood enterprise.

The company harvests surf clams and ocean quahogs using a fleet of 30 to 34 U.S.-flagged vessels in federal waters. Processing occurs across four state-of-the-art plants in Maryland, Delaware, Maine, and Massachusetts, with a co-packing facility in Virginia. These plants produce frozen and canned clam products—chowder, strips, nuggets, sauces, chopped clams, juice, stuffed clams, and concentrates—plus value-added items such as crab cakes, breaded calamari, tempura shrimp, and Super Surfer clam strips. The Milford plant is USDA and Kosher approved for soup production. Co-packing services include custom formula development, canning, portion-pack bagging, zip-locking, and klik-locking, all under HACCP and BRC-certified quality systems.

Sea Watch serves a national base of commercial and non-commercial foodservice customers, acts as a major industrial and national-brand co-pack supplier, and supplies many of the top 100 U.S. chain restaurants. An export division handles international sales, and products are also sold through retail channels.

The company emphasizes its position as the world’s largest harvester and processor of clam products and the largest independently owned, vertically integrated clam company. It works with the National Marine Fisheries Service under a quota system to manage the fishery sustainably, and its product development team brings more than 30 years of experience to new product creation.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','BRC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Offshore clam harvesting (surf clam and ocean quahog)", "Frozen and canned clam processing", "Value-added seafood production (crab cakes, breaded calamari, tempura shrimp, stuffed clams, clam strips)", "Co-packing and custom formula development", "Canning, portion-pack bagging, zip-locking, klik-locking", "Product development and bench-scale prototyping", "HACCP and BRC certified quality management", "Microbiological testing and statistical process control", "Sustainable fishery management under federal quota system", "Export sales and distribution", "Foodservice and retail distribution"], "industries": ["Foodservice (commercial and non-commercial)", "Retail seafood", "Industrial co-packing", "Restaurant chains (top 100 US)", "Export markets"], "materials": ["Surf clams", "Ocean quahog clams", "Crab", "Calamari", "Shrimp", "Other seafood ingredients"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s largest harvester and processor of clam products", "Largest independently owned and vertically integrated clam company", "Fleet of 30+ U.S.-flagged harvesting vessels", "Four HACCP- and BRC-certified manufacturing plants across four states", "USDA- and Kosher-approved soup production at Milford, DE facility"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1978 in Milford, Delaware -> /about", "Headquarters in Easton, Maryland -> /", "Independently owned and vertically integrated -> /about", "Operates 30-34 harvesting vessels -> /about, /", "Four manufacturing plants in Maryland, Delaware, Maine, Massachusetts -> /about", "Co-packing facility in Virginia -> /capabilities", "Produces frozen and canned clam products and value-added seafood -> /about", "HACCP and BRC certified facilities -> /about, /capabilities", "USDA and Kosher approved soup production at Milford plant -> /capabilities", "Serves national foodservice, co-pack, top 100 chain restaurants, export, retail -> /about", "Product development team with 30+ years experience -> /capabilities", "Sustainable fishery management with National Marine Fisheries Service -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sea Watch processes clams that are harvested by 20+ vessels in its manufacturing facilities in four state of the art plants in Maryland, Delaware, Maine, and Massachusetts.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sea-watch-international-ltd./"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sea-watch-international-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SeaTac Packaging Manufacturing Corporation operates from Puyallup, Washington, in the Greater Seattle area. The company was founded in 1994 by Scott, who identified an opportunity to better serve the Pacific Northwest fishing community with an innovative PaperWoven™ product. Starting with three employees, one bag line, and one printing press, the independently owned business set out to become the preferred supplier for seafood processors.

Today, SeaTac designs, manufactures, and delivers a range of multiwall, PaperWoven™, and flexible packaging solutions. Its capabilities span flexographic printing up to ten colors using water-based inks, coating and laminating with structures such as polypropylene, high-density polyethylene, and biaxially oriented polyamide, as well as graphic design, product development, and converting. The company runs multiple bag lines and what it describes as the widest-web, longest-repeat sustainable water-based press in the western United States, supported by large modern warehouses with 30-foot clear heights and high-bay racking for vendor-managed inventory programs.

SeaTac serves industries including food and ingredient packaging (flour, rice, evaporated dairy, potatoes, spices), agricultural products (seed, beans, peas, lentils), chemical products, and its original fishing and seafood sector. Its customer base ranges from small businesses to Fortune 500 companies, with the company emphasizing a local touch backed by a global network.

The firm differentiates itself as a vertically integrated, MBE-certified manufacturer—the only U.S. polyethylene woven producer with that designation, according to its leadership. All bags are made in America at facilities compliant with FSMA and FDA regulations and audited to the GFSI IFS PACsecure higher-level standard. A lean, just-in-time philosophy underpins what the company calls lead times, while an in-house lab and third-party testing partners support quality assurance and food safety commitments.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA COMPLIANT','FSMA compliant','GFSI IFS PACsecure higher level standard']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Multiwall bag manufacturing", "PaperWoven\u2122 packaging production", "Flexible packaging converting", "Flexographic printing (up to 10 colors, water-based inks)", "Coating and laminating (PP, HDPE, BOPA structures)", "Graphic design and prepress services", "Product development and engineering", "Quality assurance and food safety testing", "Field support and operational consulting", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI)", "Just-in-time (JIT) manufacturing", "Warehousing and distribution"], "industries": ["Fishing and seafood", "Food and beverage", "Agriculture", "Chemicals"], "materials": ["Polypropylene (PP)", "High-density polyethylene (HDPE)", "Biaxially oriented polyamide (BOPA)", "Polyethylene (woven)", "Paper (multiwall)", "Biaxially oriented polypropylene (BOPP)", "Woven polypropylene", "Woven polyethylene"], "equipment": ["Bag lines (multiple)", "Wide-web water-based flexographic printing press", "Coating and laminating equipment", "High-bay racking system", "Warehouses with 30-foot clear heights"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing from design to converted packaging", "Only U.S. polyethylene woven bag manufacturer with MBE certification", "Sustainable water-based flexographic printing on the widest web and longest repeat in the western U.S.", "Lean and just-in-time manufacturing delivering industry-leading lead times"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 by Scott with three employees, one bag line, one printing press -> /about", "Located in Puyallup, Washington (Greater Seattle area) -> /", "Independently owned, MBE certified -> /, /services", "Manufactures multiwall, PaperWoven\u2122, flexible packaging -> /", "Flexographic printing up to 10 colors, water-based inks -> /services", "Coatings and poly liners in PP, HDPE, BOPA structures -> db", "Serves fishing/seafood, food, agricultural, chemical industries -> /, /products", "FSMA/FDA compliant, GFSI IFS PACsecure higher level -> /, /services", "Vertically integrated, only US polyethylene woven manufacturer with MBE certification -> /, /services", "Lean/JIT manufacturing, industry-leading lead times -> /services", "Warehouses with 30'' clear heights, high bay racking -> /services", "Graphic design, product development, quality assurance, field support, VMI -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SeaTac Packaging designs, manufactures, and delivers a wide variety of multiwall, PaperWoven\u2122, and flexible packaging.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='seatac-packaging-manufacturing-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Segue Manufacturing Services operates from North Billerica, Massachusetts, just outside Boston. The company established operations in 1991 with the goal of getting customers'' products to market while exceeding expectations. It is a U.S.-owned and operated business backed by private equity firm Cornell Capital. In 2024, Segue joined with Lorom and In-Tech Electronics to form Lisconn, a combined entity reflecting a shared 100 years of experience in electronics, engineering, and interconnect innovation.

As a global contract manufacturer, Segue integrates engineering services with manufacturing operations in Boston, Tijuana (Mexico), and Xiamen (China), plus partner factories in Malaysia and India. The company provides capabilities scaling from sub-assembly level to complete end-to-end manufacturing, including prototype fabrication, new product introduction, domestic stocking and replenishment, and quality systems. Its vertically integrated model combines local engineering and customer service with cost-effective global production.

Segue serves OEMs and Tier 1 electronics manufacturing services customers across highly regulated sectors. Its industry expertise spans medical devices and healthcare, industrial automation and robotics, capital equipment and semiconductor, industrial and IoT, instrumentation, energy and environmental, and aerospace and defense. The company focuses on complex electronic products where it has deep assembly experience.

Segue differentiates itself through right-shoring flexibility, offering customers the benefits of local engineering support combined with manufacturing where it makes economic sense. The company emphasizes proactive customer service, real-time testing systems, and common manufacturing platforms that enable rapid transitions without compromising quality. It only takes on projects where it has the experience to deliver successfully, aiming to lower inventory carrying costs while maintaining exceptional delivery performance.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','IATF 16949','MedAccred']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract manufacturing", "Engineering services", "Prototype fabrication", "New product introduction (NPI)", "Domestic stocking and replenishment", "Quality systems management", "Sub-assembly manufacturing", "End-to-end manufacturing", "Supply chain management", "Real-time testing systems", "Common manufacturing platforms", "Inspection and test platforms"], "industries": ["Medical Devices & Healthcare", "Industrial Automation & Robotics", "Capital Equipment & Semiconductor", "Industrial & IoT", "Instrumentation", "Energy & Environmental", "Aerospace & Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low-to-medium volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Right-shoring options with manufacturing in USA, Mexico, China, Malaysia, and India", "Local engineering and service paired with cost-effective global manufacturing", "Vertically integrated capabilities that lower inventory carrying costs", "Focus only on assemblies where the company has deep experience", "Proactive, responsive customer service with real-time project visibility"], "facts_used": ["Established operations in 1991 -> /about-us", "U.S. owned and operated global contract manufacturer -> /", "Manufacturing operations in Boston, Tijuana, Xiamen, Malaysia, India -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, IATF 16949, MedAccred -> /"