UPDATE companies SET description='Shermco Industries, headquartered in Irving, Texas, was founded in 1974 by Pete Sherman. The company began by repairing generators for aircraft during the Vietnam War, with Sherman recalling that at one point nearly every B-52 in the U.S. fleet had a generator serviced by Shermco. That dedication to quality and personal service turned single-job clients into long-term partners, fueling the firm''s growth into a nationwide electrical services provider.

Today Shermco operates as an electrical services platform delivering field, shop, and engineering & control services. Its 700-plus NETA-certified technicians and 230-plus engineers work from 41 service centers across the United States and Canada. Core offerings include NETA-accredited power system testing and maintenance, transformer services, protection and control engineering, rotating machinery repair, wind turbine support, motor and generator rewinds up to 15 kV, circuit breaker refurbishment, disaster recovery, and electrical safety training. The motor shops hold ISO 9001:2015 and EASA accreditation, while breaker technicians are PEARL certified.

The company serves data centers, utilities, oil and gas producers, chemical plants, industrial manufacturers, and the growing wind energy sector. Clients in these markets rely on Shermco to maintain continuous operation and avoid downtime, leveraging the firm''s expertise in NERC, ERCOT, PJM, and CAISO compliance, interconnection studies, and field engineering support.

Shermco states its purpose is to provide specialty technical expertise that safely and reliably powers essential businesses and communities. It emphasizes a safety-first culture where every employee can stop work without reprisal, and it positions itself as North America''s largest and fastest-growing NETA-accredited testing organization.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','NETA accredited','EASA accredited','PEARL certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical power system maintenance", "NETA acceptance and maintenance testing", "Protection and control testing", "Transformer services and oil sampling", "Rotating machinery field services", "Wind field services", "Engineering assessments for compliance (NERC, ERCOT, PJM, CAISO)", "Interconnection studies", "Motor and generator repair (rewinds, machining, balancing)", "Breaker refurbishment (primary/secondary injection testing, overhauls, remanufacturing, retrofits)", "Disaster recovery services", "Electrical safety training (NFPA 70B)", "Laser alignment services", "Arc flash services", "Compliance engineering services", "Up-tower machining"], "industries": ["Data centers", "Utilities", "Oil and gas", "Chemicals", "Industrial manufacturing", "Wind energy", "Renewables"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["North America''s largest NETA-accredited electrical testing organization", "24/7 emergency field service with 41 locations across the U.S. and Canada", "ISO 9001:2015 and EASA accredited motor and generator repair shops", "PEARL-certified circuit breaker refurbishment and mobile breaker shops", "700+ NETA-certified technicians and 230+ engineers on staff"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 by Pete Sherman -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Irving, Texas -> /", "700+ NETA-certified technicians -> /about-us", "230+ engineers -> /about-us", "41 service centers in U.S. and Canada -> /about-us", "NETA accredited electrical testing organization -> /ab