UPDATE companies SET description='Signature Cable, Inc. was founded in 2002 and is headquartered in Cranston, Rhode Island. The company operates a domestic manufacturing facility in Rhode Island, about 10 minutes from Providence, and also partners with suppliers in Hong Kong and China.

The company specializes in molded cables, custom wire and cable harnesses, and electro-mechanical box build assemblies for original equipment manufacturers. It offers full production capabilities including wire harness production, cable assemblies, molded cable assemblies, prototyping, engineering, and R&D support.

Its customer base spans the military, medical, industrial, aerospace, security, transportation, semiconductor, automation, and homeland security sectors. The company serves OEMs across these industries, building everything from single cables to thousands of units on payment terms.

Signature Cable differentiates itself through its ISO 9001:2015 certification, UL and Canadian UL listings, RoHS compliance, and adherence to IPC 610/620 Class I, II, and III standards as well as MIL-STD-45662. The company emphasizes competitive pricing, low overhead, fast turnaround times, a newly implemented ERP system, and lean manufacturing practices such as 5S to drive efficiency and cost savings.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL Listed','Canadian UL Listed','RoHS Compliant','IPC 610 Class I, II, III','IPC 620 Class I, II, III','MIL-STD-45662']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire harness production", "Wire harness assemblies", "Custom cable assemblies", "Molded cable assemblies", "Electro-mechanical box build assemblies", "Prototyping and engineering", "Prototype design", "R&D support", "Continuity testing", "Component detection", "Capacitor checks", "Resistor checks", "Diode testing", "Twisted pair testing", "Hi-pot testing", "Crimp/pull testing"], "industries": ["Military", "Medical", "Industrial", "Aerospace", "Security", "Transportation", "Semiconductor", "Automation", "Homeland Security"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to low/medium volume (high-mix)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum annual spend or order size", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with UL/Canadian UL listings", "Lean manufacturing (5S) and ERP-driven efficiency", "Domestic manufacturing in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Cranston, Rhode Island -> /about", "Domestic manufacturing facility in Rhode Island -> /about", "Partnerships with suppliers in Hong Kong and China -> /about", "Specializes in molded cables, custom wire and cable harnesses, electro-mechanical box build assemblies -> /about", "High-mix, low-to-medium volume production -> /about", "No minimum annual spend or order size -> /about, /", "Quick-turn prototypes in 24-48 hours -> /about", "Industries served: military, medical, industrial, aerospace, security, transportation, semiconductor, automation, homeland security -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality, db", "UL & Canadian UL Listed -> /quality", "RoHS Compliant -> /quality, db", "IPC 610 & 620 Class I, II, III standards -> /quality", "MIL-STD-45662 -> /quality", "Lean manufacturing (5S) and ERP system -> /quality", "Competitive pricing, low overhead, fast turnaround -> /, /about", "Company type: contract manufacturer -> /about", "Makes physical products (wire harnesses, cable assemblies) -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Signature Cable Inc. is a global electronics contract manufacturing company specializing in molded cables, custom wire and cable harnesses as well as electro-mechanical box build assemblies for OEM''s.", "founded_year": "2002", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/signature-cable-inc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='signature-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Single Source Medical was founded in 2001 in Churubusco, Indiana, and operates a 21,350-square-foot facility with a team of 40. The company is led by President Jordan Nicodemus and focuses exclusively on contract manufacturing for the orthopedic sector.

The shop provides end-to-end production of implants and surgical instruments, running Swiss-type turning (20–32 mm bar capacity), 5-axis mill-turn, 5-axis milling (Matsuura MX-330 and DMG Mori), wire EDM, laser marking, multi-stage ultrasonic cleaning, citric passivation, deburring, finishing, CMM inspection, and final assembly. All processes are performed in-house under an ISO 13485:2016 quality system with FDA registration.

Customers are orthopedic OEMs in the spine, trauma, and upper- and lower-extremity markets. Typical components include bone screws, trauma plates, spinal cages, acetabular shells, trial instruments, and broaches, machined from titanium 6Al-4V, cobalt chrome, 17-4 and 316L stainless steels, and medical-grade polymers.

The company emphasizes a “wrap-around” service model — DFM feedback, fast-turn prototyping, vendor-managed inventory, and packaging/labeling — to shrink the supply chain. Its stated philosophy balances being a supplier of choice, an employer of choice, and an investment of choice, with a culture built on responsiveness, validated processes, and accountability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Swiss-type turning (20\u201332 mm bar capacity)", "5-axis mill-turn / live tooling", "5-axis milling", "Wire EDM", "Laser marking (UDI, lot numbers)", "Ultrasonic cleaning", "Citric passivation (ASTM A967)", "Deburring & finishing (tumbling, bead blast, hand polish)", "CMM & vision inspection", "Assembly (sub-assembly and final assembly)", "Packaging & labeling", "Vendor-managed inventory", "DFM feedback", "Prototyping", "Saw cutting", "Thread rolling (planned)", "Heat treat (outsourced)", "Anodization (outsourced)", "Chrome coating (outsourced)", "PVD coating (outsourced)", "TiN coating (outsourced)", "Electropolishing (outsourced)", "Grinding (outsourced)", "Overmolding (outsourced)"], "industries": ["Orthopedic implants", "Orthopedic instruments", "Spine", "Trauma", "Upper extremity", "Lower extremity", "Medical devices"], "materials": ["Titanium (CP & 6Al-4V)", "Cobalt Chrome (CoCr)", "Stainless Steel (17-4, 316L, 455)", "Tool & Carbon Steel", "Aluminum", "UHMW", "Radel", "Acetal / Delrin"], "equipment": ["Star Swiss platforms", "Matsuura MX-330", "DMG Mori 5-axis", "Fanuc Robocut wire EDM", "Zeiss Contura CMM", "Keyence vision system", "Surface profilometers", "Fiber laser marking system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Wrap-around services (DFM, prototyping, assembly, packaging, VMI) performed in-house", "Full traceability from raw material heat lot through final inspection", "Responsive front-end engineering with validated back-end processes", "Three-pillar philosophy: supplier, employer, and investment of choice"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> db", "40 employees -> db", "Headquarters Churubusco, Indiana -> db", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /", "FDA registered -> /", "21,350 sq ft facility -> /", "Swiss-type turning, 5-axis milling, wire EDM, laser marking, cleaning, passivation, assembly -> /", "Materials: Titanium, Cobalt Chrome, Stainless Steel, etc. -> /", "Industries: orthopedic spine, trauma, upper/lower extremity -> /", "Equipment: Star Swiss, Matsuura MX-330, DMG Mori, Fanuc Robocut, Zeiss Contura CMM, Keyence vision -> /", "President Jordan Nicodemus -> /", "Three commitments philosophy -> /", "Vendor-managed inventory, DFM, prototyping -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Single Source Medical (SSM) is a contract manufacturer dedicated exclusively to the orthopedic industry \u2014 serving the spine, trauma, and upper & lower extremity markets.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "40", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='single-source-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Southeastern Kentucky Rehabilitation Industries (SEKRI) was established in 1971 in Corbin, Kentucky, as a non-profit organization dedicated to creating employment opportunities for people with mental and physical disabilities in the Appalachian region. At a time when few jobs existed for individuals with significant disabilities, government agencies and school systems began referring clients to SEKRI for basic work-skills training.

Today SEKRI operates seven facilities across Kentucky and Tennessee, employing more than 700 people. The organization runs spreading and cutting operations on Gerber equipment and provides a full range of sewing services—from flat-lock single-needle stitching to embroidery—producing military apparel, commercial textiles, and partner products such as coats for Operation Warm. In addition to manufacturing, SEKRI offers contract packaging, fulfillment, warehousing, inventory management, and logistics, shipping over 50,000 units per week from its combined plants. The company also deploys teams to prepare and wrap training-range facilities with site-specific vinyl for military exercises.

SEKRI’s primary customers are federal and defense agencies purchasing through the AbilityOne program, which requires a workforce of at least 75 percent disabled individuals. Key accounts include the U.S. military for sewn goods and Lockheed Martin, for which SEKRI manages vendor‑owned inventory and delivers orders in as little as two hours, earning a Platinum Vendor Supplier Rating. The non-profit also serves commercial partners such as Operation Warm and has supported training-range construction for soldier readiness programs.

SEKRI’s founding mission—to provide competitive, gainful employment for persons with disabilities—remains its central differentiator. The organization maintains ISO 9001:2015 certification and a quality policy targeting 100 percent customer requirements and on-time delivery. Its AbilityOne designation and non-profit structure allow it to reinvest revenue directly into workforce development, including on‑site GED programs, veteran services, and rehabilitation referrals.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Spreading and cutting (Gerber technology)", "Sewing: flat-lock single needle, embroidery, and other stitching", "Contract packaging and fulfillment", "Warehousing, inventory management, and logistics", "Training range facility preparation and vinyl wrapping", "Community rehabilitation referral services", "Veteran employee services", "On-site GED and adult education", "Textile product manufacturing", "Engineering and manufacturing of textile products", "Vendor managed inventory", "Shipping and distribution"], "industries": ["Defense / Military", "Government (AbilityOne program)", "Aerospace (Lockheed Martin)", "Non-profit / Social services (Operation Warm)", "Textile / Apparel manufacturing", "Training and simulation (training range facilities)"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Gerber spreading and cutting systems"], "volume": "Over 50,000 products per week", "lead_time": "As little as 2 hours for vendor-managed inventory orders (Lockheed Martin)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AbilityOne program: minimum 75% disabled workforce", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "Ships 50,000+ products weekly from seven facilities", "Two-hour delivery on vendor-managed inventory for Lockheed Martin", "Non-profit reinvesting in workforce development (GED, veteran services)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 in Corbin, Kentucky -> /about", "Non-profit providing employment for persons with disabilities -> /about", "Operates seven facilities, employs over 700 individuals -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about", "Ships over 50,000 products weekly -> /", "Gerber technology for spreading and cutting -> /", "Sewing services from flat-lock single needle to embroidery -> /", "Contract packaging & fulfillment, warehouse, inventory management & logistics -> /", "Vendor managed inventory for Lockheed Martin with 2-hour delivery -> /about", "Training range facilities preparation with vinyl wrap -> /about", "AbilityOne program (75% disabled workforce) -> /about", "Lockheed Martin Platinum Vendor Supplier Rating -> /about", "Partnership with Operation Warm -> db", "Headquarters in Corbin, Kentucky -> /about", "Executive team includes Leo Miller, Norm Bradley, etc. -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SEKRI ships over 50,000 products each week from our combined facilities.", "founded_year": "1971", "employee_count": "700+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='southeastern-kentucky-rehabilitation-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Southern Energy Management was founded in 2001 in Raleigh, North Carolina. The company began as a building performance and solar installation firm focused on helping builders and homeowners improve energy efficiency.

The firm provides residential and commercial solar photovoltaic and battery storage installation, along with building performance services such as HERS ratings, code compliance testing, green program certification (including LEED and ENERGY STAR), zero energy consulting, air sealing, and HVAC grading. It operates as a certified Tesla Powerwall installer and reports more than 3,000 completed solar and battery projects. The company serves single-family builders, multifamily developers, commercial businesses, non-profits, and architects across North Carolina, South Carolina, and nationally for multifamily projects.

Its customer base includes homeowners seeking solar and battery systems, production and custom home builders needing energy code compliance and performance verification, multifamily developers pursuing green certifications and incentive guidance, and commercial organizations looking for turn-key solar solutions. The company also works with architects on building performance modeling and certification.

Southern Energy Management was started to address the complexity and cost of unexpected home performance problems during construction. The company says it helps builders solve those challenges to deliver more efficient homes profitably and on schedule, without headaches during or after the build.', certifications=ARRAY['LEED','ENERGY STAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar PV installation", "Commercial solar PV installation", "Battery storage installation", "HERS rating and code compliance testing", "Green building certification (LEED, ENERGY STAR, DOE Zero Energy Ready)", "Zero energy consulting", "Air sealing services", "HVAC grading", "Building performance inspections", "Energy modeling (ASHRAE)", "Multifamily sustainability consulting", "Incentive and grant guidance", "Builder trade onboarding and training", "Sales and marketing support for builders"], "industries": ["Single-family home building", "Multifamily construction", "Commercial solar", "Residential solar", "Energy efficiency consulting", "Green building certification", "Architecture and design"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified Tesla Powerwall installer", "3,000+ solar and battery installations completed", "HERS ratings, code testing, and green certification for builders in NC and SC", "Turn-key commercial solar solutions with grant writing and financial partnership", "Nationwide multifamily green building consulting and incentive guidance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> db", "Headquarters Raleigh, NC -> db", "Certifications LEED, ENERGY STAR -> db", "Capabilities list -> db", "3,000+ solar & battery customers -> homepage", "Certified Tesla Powerwall Installer -> homepage", "Services: residential solar, commercial solar, builder energy services, multifamily & commercial energy services -> homepage", "Industries served: homeowners, builders, multifamily developers, commercial businesses, architects -> homepage", "Why: help builders solve home performance challenges to build efficient homes profitably and on schedule -> description"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "North Carolina Solar Installer & Building Performance Experts", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='southern-energy-management' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Southwest Plastics Co. The company is led by owners Tom and Rob Jorgensen, who emphasize direct customer access and a commitment to onshore manufacturing.

The company specializes in high-precision plastic components produced through thermoset molding, thermoplastic injection molding, transfer molding, compression molding, and rubber molding. Supported by in-house CNC machining, tooling, assembly, pad printing, testing, and packaging, Southwest Plastics reports producing millions of custom, high-tolerance parts annually for runs ranging from several thousand to millions of units.

Its customer base spans aerospace, military and defense, automotive, medical device, electronics, food and beverage, power generation, oil and gas, OEMs, and marine and maritime sectors. The firm serves both large aerospace contractors and small manufacturers seeking custom component development.

Southwest Plastics differentiates itself through its AS9100 certification, a focus on intellectual property protection, material expertise built over three generations, and a ''white-glove'' service model that balances capacity for large projects with personalized attention. The company also highlights its role in reshoring initiatives and faster turnaround times for domestic production.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoset molding", "Thermoplastic injection molding", "Transfer molding", "Compression molding", "Rubber molding", "CNC machining", "Tooling", "Assembly", "Pad printing", "Testing", "Packaging", "Delivery", "Engineering services", "Silk screen"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Military & Defense", "Automotive", "Medical device", "Electronics", "Food & beverage", "Power generation", "Oil & gas", "OEMs", "Marine & maritime", "Telecom", "Healthcare"], "materials": ["Thermoset plastics", "Thermoplastic plastics", "Delrin", "Ryton", "Ultem", "ABS"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Several thousand to millions of units annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AS9100 certified quality management system", "Millions of high-tolerance parts produced annually", "Three generations of family ownership and material expertise", "IP protection and onshore manufacturing commitment", "White-glove service with direct owner access"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> db", "Headquarters Glendora, California -> db", "AS9100 certification -> db, /services", "Family-owned, three generations of hands-on ownership -> /about", "Owners Tom and Rob Jorgensen -> /about", "Processes: thermoset molding, thermoplastic injection molding, transfer molding, compression molding, rubber molding -> /services", "Support services: CNC machining, tooling, assembly, pad printing, testing, packaging, delivery, engineering services, silk screen -> /services", "Annual volume millions of parts, runs from several thousand to millions -> /services", 