UPDATE companies SET description='Spectra-Tech Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1998 in Batavia, Ohio, about 15 miles east of Cincinnati. The company began with a team of technical experts who had spent years in printed circuit board manufacturing, aiming to give customers insight into manufacturability issues and deliver lower-cost, higher-quality assemblies than other PCB manufacturers.

Today the firm operates as a full-service electronic contract manufacturer. Its facility runs four high-speed Fuji SMT lines, two ERSA selective soldering machines, a SPEA 4030 flying-probe in-circuit tester, X-ray inspection, and a Stoelting aqueous wash system. Services span surface-mount and through-hole assembly, conformal coating, wire harness and cable assembly, overmolding, box build, and engineering support including design-for-manufacturability reviews, prototyping, and documentation control via Aegis Factory Logix software.

The company serves customers in industrial controls and water monitoring, and its ISO 13485:2016 certification qualifies it for medical-device work. Each client is assigned a dedicated program manager, and Spectra-Tech offers customized Kanban and stocking programs, supply-chain management with vendor consignment and EDI, and full program management from introduction through delivery.

Spectra-Tech emphasizes its quality system—ISO 9001:2015 certified, IPC-A-610, J-STD-001, and IPC-7711/7721 trained personnel, plus RoHS-compliant processes—as the foundation for consistent, defect-free production across prototype, low-volume, and high-volume runs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','RoHS','IPC-A-610','J-STD-001','IPC-7711/7721','IPC CEPM','SMTA Corporate Member']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface Mount Assembly (SMT)", "Through-hole Assembly", "Selective Soldering", "Conformal Coating", "In-Circuit Testing (ICT) / Flying Probe", "X-Ray Inspection", "Water Wash / Aqueous Cleaning", "Wire Harness Assembly", "Cable Assembly", "Overmolding", "Box Build / Final Assembly", "Engineering Services", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Prototyping", "Program Management", "Supply Chain Management", "Kanban & Stocking Programs", "Documentation Control & Process Engineering", "BOM to Layout Verification", "Revision Control / Paperless Documentation", "Thermal Profiling", "Fixture Development", "IPC Certified Training (IPC-A-610, J-STD-001)", "RoHS Compliant Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Industrial Controls", "Water Monitoring", "Medical Devices"], "materials": ["FR-4 PCBs", "Lead-free solder", "Conformal coating materials", "Wire and cable", "Overmolding compounds"], "equipment": ["Fuji high-speed SMT lines (4)", "SPEA 4030 flying probe tester", "ERSA selective soldering machines (2)", "X-ray inspection system", "Stoelting water wash system", "Aegis Factory Logix software"], "volume": "Prototype, low to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated program manager assigned to every customer", "Custom Kanban and stocking programs for inventory turns and just-in-time delivery", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) review included as a value-added service", "Four high-speed Fuji SMT lines with X-ray and flying-probe in-circuit test", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certified for medical and commerci