UPDATE companies SET description='Standard Components LLC was founded in 2001 in Sterling Heights, Michigan, as a privately owned business specializing in aerospace, defense, and automotive fixturing and tooling. In 2016 the company was acquired by the private equity firm Summit Equity Group, which has since invested in expanding its operations.

The company designs, builds, and certifies checking fixtures, holding fixtures, transport fixtures, and assembly tooling for applications ranging from aircraft wings and doors to fighter jet components and automotive EV battery trays. Its 44,500-square-foot facility includes a climate-controlled certification room, two 10-ton crane bays, weld and paint stations, and both 3-axis and 5-axis milling centers, enabling vertically integrated production from design through final inspection.

Standard Components serves commercial and corporate aircraft manufacturers such as Gulfstream and Bombardier, defense primes including Lockheed Martin, and automotive OEMs and Tier One suppliers like General Motors and Stellantis. Programs cover inspection and assembly fixtures for airframes, mission-critical defense hardware, and automotive interiors, body panels, and electrification components.

The firm emphasizes a turn-key approach that spans quote inception, design, build, and final certification, backed by AS9100 Rev.D and ISO 9001:2015 quality systems and ITAR registration.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100 Rev.D','ITAR registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Checking fixture design and build", "Holding fixture design and build", "Transport fixture design and build", "Assembly tooling design and build", "CMM checking fixture certification", "Weld fixture fabrication", "Vacuum and drill jig fabrication", "Assembly fixture fabrication", "3-axis CNC milling", "5-axis CNC milling", "Welding", "Painting", "Engineering services", "Quality inspection and certification", "Turn-key program management", "On-site installation"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Fixture plank", "Wood", "Plastics", "Acrylic", "Laminates", "Foam"], "equipment": ["3-axis milling centers", "5-axis milling centers", "10-ton crane bays (two)", "Weld stations", "Paint stations", "Climate-controlled certification room"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turn-key program delivery from design through on-site installation", "Vertically integrated manufacturing with in-house certification", "Climate-controlled facility with dedicated CMM certification room", "3-axis and 5-axis milling capacity for complex tooling", "AS9100 Rev.D, ISO 9001:2015, and ITAR compliance"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> db", "Headquarters in Sterling Heights, Michigan -> db", "Privately owned, acquired by Summit Equity Group in 2016 -> /", "44,500 sq ft facility with climate-controlled certification room, two 10-ton crane bays, weld and paint stations, 3-axis and 5-axis milling centers -> /about", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, AS9100 Rev.D, ITAR registered -> /about", "Customers: Lockheed Martin, Gulfstream, Bombardier, General Motors, Stellantis -> /about", "Materials: steel, aluminum, fixture plank