UPDATE companies SET description='Star Plastics, LLC, headquartered in Millwood, West Virginia, traces its origins to 1988 when parent company SDR Plastics was formed as a post-industrial recycling operation. SDR processed materials destined for landfill, returning them to the polymer market. Ten years later, Star Plastics emerged as a custom compounder, building on that recycling heritage. The company now operates facilities in Ravenswood, West Virginia; Evansville, Indiana; Calhoun, Georgia; and Shandong, China.

The company specializes in custom color compounding, toll compounding, and polymer sourcing for engineering-grade thermoplastics, with a focus on ABS, polycarbonates, polycarbonate alloys, and nylons. Its full-service on-site laboratories develop, test, and formulate custom plastic compounds, offering lot-to-lot consistency and real-time in-process monitoring of physical properties, color, and flame retardancy. Star also provides recycled-content materials up to 100% classification, including pre-consumer, post-consumer, ITE, and ocean-bound grades. The firm emphasizes batches of any size, supported by over 35 years of tolling experience.

Star serves automotive, electronics/electrical, and hybrid vehicle industries, as well as large resin manufacturers. Its materials are UL-recognized and certified for automotive applications. The PolymerVault division sources and supplies resins of any grade or form globally.

Founded on a mission to reclaim plastic waste, Star differentiates itself through a 98.6% material satisfaction rate over three years, weekly continuous-improvement meetings, and a comprehensive analytical lab capable of Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy, differential scanning calorimetry, and a suite of mechanical and flammability tests.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom color compounding", "Toll compounding", "Plastic processing", "Polymer sourcing (PolymerVault)", "Engineering-grade thermoplastic compounding (ABS, PC, PC alloys, nylons)", "Recycled-content compounding", "On-site analytical lab testing", "Real-time in-process monitoring", "Quality management (ISO 9001)", "Lot-to-lot consistency control", "Custom formulated resin development", "Material satisfaction tracking"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Electronics/electrical", "Hybrid vehicles", "Resin manufacturers"], "materials": ["ABS", "Polycarbonates", "Polycarbonate alloys", "Nylons", "Recycled content (pre-consumer, post-consumer, ITE, ocean-bound)"], "equipment": ["Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy", "Thermal Gravimetric Analysis", "Differential Scanning Calorimetry (DSC)", "Melt Index", "Notched Izod Impact Test", "Spectrophotometer", "Heat Deflection Temperature", "Low Temperature Impact", "Tensile Properties", "Flexural Properties", "Gloss Measurement", "Vicat Softening", "Ash Content", "Flame Retardant Testing", "Specific Gravity", "Gardner Impact", "Moisture Analysis", "Correlated Haze"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lot-to-lot consistency in custom color compounding", "Real-time in-process monitoring of physical properties, color, and flame retardancy", "On-site analytical lab with full testing capabilities (FTIR, DSC, Izod, etc.)", "Up to 100% recycled-content materials with certified classifications", "Over 35 years of toll compounding experience"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Millwood, WV with facilities in Ravenswood WV, Evansville IN, Calhoun GA, Shandong China -> homepage", "Founded 1988 as SDR Plastics recycling company -> /about", "Custom color compounding, toll compounding, polymer sourcing -> homepage", "Focus on ABS, polycarbonates, polycarbonate alloys, nylons -> homepage, /about", "On-site lab with listed test capabilities -> /quality", "Real-time in-process monitoring -> homepage", "98.6% material satisfaction rate over three years -> homepage, /quality", "ISO 9001 certified at designated facilities -> /quality, db", "ISO 14001, IATF 16949 from db -> db", "UL-recognized products, automotive certified -> homepage", "Recycled content up to 100% with classifications -> homepage", "PolymerVault division for resin sourcing -> homepage", "Over 35 years tolling experience -> homepage", "Weekly continuous improvement meetings -> /quality", "Merger with Trivalence Technologies -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Star Plastics\u00ae is an industry leading compounder of engineering-grade thermoplastics", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='star-plastics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Steel Craft Technologies was founded in 2001 and operates from two locations in the Grand Rapids, Michigan area: a headquarters in Belmont and a second facility in Grand Rapids. The company began as a steel service center focused on plate processing and has grown to serve the die, mold, and heavy-equipment markets.

Today the company runs two facilities totaling 160,000 square feet of manufacturing space, including an 80,000-square-foot CNC machine shop, and employs approximately 125 people. Its core capabilities cover steel plate processing—oxy-fuel and plasma burning, Blanchard and Mattison grinding, surface milling, and precision CNC machining—as well as fabrication of heavy steel weldments, stress relieving, and media blasting. The shop produces die sets, ejector box assemblies, tooling plates, bolster plates, die parallels, mold rails, and custom weldments such as machine bases and press frames.

Steel Craft serves the die and mold industry, OEM and heavy-equipment manufacturers, and the mining sector.

The company emphasizes on-time delivery, ISO 9001:2015 quality management, and ITAR compliance. It also highlights its in-house steel inventory, AWS-certified welders (FCAW 3G per AWS D1.1), and a commitment to recycling 100 percent of mill chips and grinding sludge.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AWS D1.1','ITAR Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Steel plate processing", "Oxy-fuel cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Blanchard grinding", "Mattison surface grinding", "Surface milling", "Precision CNC machining", "Stress relieving", "Media blasting (shot blasting)", "Fabrication and welding (FCAW, AWS D1.1)", "Die set manufacturing", "Ejector box assembly", "Tooling plate manufacturing", "Bolster plate manufacturing", "Die parallels machining", "Mold rails machining", "Nitro plate assembly", "Industrial weldments", "Machine base fabrication", "Press frame fabrication", "CAD/CAM programming", "Inventory management"], "industries": ["Die and mold", "OEM and heavy equipment", "Mining"], "materials": ["Carbon steel plate", "Alloy steel plate", "Steel plate (various grades)"], "equipment": ["Oxy-Fuel Multi-Torch Cutting Tables", "Omega Exactus Pro Tool Measuring Machine", "Blanchard grinders", "Mattison grinders", "CNC machines", "CAD/CAM cutting machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> db", "Headquarters in Belmont, Michigan -> db", "Two facilities totaling 160,000 sq ft -> /", "125 employees across two locations -> /", "Over 25 years experience in steel service center industry -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /services", "ITAR Compliant -> /, /services", "AWS certified welders (FCAW 3G per AWS D1.1) -> /services", "PMA membership -> /, /services", "Oxy-Fuel Multi-Torch Cutting Tables added May 2020 -> /", "Omega Exactus Pro Tool Measuring Machine added Nov 2019 -> /", "Services: burning, grinding, machining, fabrication, stress relieving, media blasting -> /services", "Die & mold industry focus: die sets, ejector boxes, tooling plates, bolster plates, die parallels, mold rails -> /services", "Fabrication: industrial weldments, machine bases, press frames -> /services", "OEM/Heavy equipment: in-house steel inventory, CAD file acceptance -> /services", "Recycles 100% of mill chips and grinding sludge -> /", "Locations: Belmont, MI and Grand Rapids, MI -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our 80,000 sq. ft. CNC machine shop specializes in the manufacturing of die sets, ejector box assemblies, tooling plates, and bolster plates.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "125", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR Compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='steel-craft-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Steel Technologies LLC is headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky. The company was founded in 1971 by Merwin J. Ray, with its first plant in Eminence, Kentucky. After trading on NASDAQ for 22 years, it became a wholly owned subsidiary of Mitsui & Co. (USA), Inc. in 2007. In 2010, Mitsui formed a joint venture with Nucor Corporation, known as NuMit, which now owns 100% of the company. Steel Technologies operates as an independent business under this ownership.

The company processes steel and aluminum across 32 locations in North America, shipping over 3.8 million tons annually to more than 2,500 customer ship-to locations worldwide, with annual sales exceeding $2.5 billion. Its value-added processing includes pre-painted and specialty coated steel up to 0.625 inches thick, high-heat products, and cold metal products. Capabilities extend to supply chain management, logistics, vendor-managed inventory, and technical support, all accessible through a 24/7 customer portal.

Steel Technologies serves the automotive industry, supplying all automotive grades and in exposed blanking for U.S. automakers. Its customer base includes industrial manufacturers across North America, such as Calstrip Industries in Mira Loma, California. The company’s strategically located facilities near railways, waterways, and airports provide cost-saving logistics advantages.

The company emphasizes a customer-driven, growth-oriented culture, citing its dedicated team, extensive capabilities, and broad geographic reach as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','IATF 16949','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Steel processing", "Aluminum processing", "Pre-painted and specialty coated steel", "High-heat steel products", "Cold metal products", "Exposed blanking", "Value-added processing", "Supply chain management", "Logistics and transportation", "Vendor managed inventory", "Technical support", "24/7 customer portal access"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial manufacturing"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Pre-painted steel", "Specialty coated steel", "High-heat steel", "Cold metal products"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 3.8 million tons annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["32 processing locations across North America", "Over 3.8 million tons shipped annually", "24/7 customer portal with vendor-managed inventory", "Strategically located facilities with rail, water, and air access", "Customer-driven team with broad geographic reach"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1971 by Merwin J. Ray -> db", "First plant in Eminence, KY -> db", "Headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky -> db", "Owned by NuMit (Nucor-Mitsui joint venture) -> db", "32 locations across North America -> page \"/\"", "Over 3.8 million tons shipped annually -> page \"/\"", "Over 2500 customer ship-to locations internationally -> page \"/\"", "Over $2.5 billion in annual sales -> page \"/\"", "Products: pre-painted and specialty coated steel up to 0.625 inches thick -> db", "High heat products -> db", "Cold metal products in Ottawa, OH -> db", "Serves automotive industry, all automotive grades, exposed blanking -> db", "Calstrip Industries in Mira Loma, CA -> db", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 14001, IATF 16949, ROHS -> db", "24/7 customer portal, vendor managed inventory, technical support -> page \"/\"", "Su