UPDATE companies SET description='TE Wire & Cable LLC operates from Saddle Brook, New Jersey, where it has manufactured thermocouple and specialty wire since 1941. The business originated as the Wire and Cable Division of Thermo Electric Corporation, created to supply high‑quality wire for temperature‑measurement markets spanning cryogenic to 1,300 °C applications. Today it is a subsidiary of Marmon Wire & Cable, a Berkshire Hathaway company.

The company produces a full line of thermocouple wire and extension cable from iron‑ and nickel‑based alloys and copper, with insulation ranging from PVC to CEFIR® ceramic fiber braids. It also provides custom cable assembly, wire assembly, and box‑build services. An in‑house calibration laboratory, directly certified by NIST and accredited to ISO/IEC 17025:2017, calibrates and matches wire from ‑320 °F to 2,400 °F, supporting compliance with AMS2750, ASTM E220, BAC5621 and other aerospace and industrial specifications.

Customers include aerospace composites manufacturers, industrial OEMs, steel and aluminum metallurgy plants, medical device makers, aviation engine test facilities, and power generation operators. The wire serves temperature‑sensing and control circuits in environments from cryogenic furnaces to high‑temperature engine testing.

TE Wire & Cable emphasizes its position as the world’s largest thermocouple wire manufacturer, citing short lead times, competitive pricing, and a calibration program verified against U.S., British, and Dutch national standards as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['NADCAP','ISO 9001:2015','ISO/IEC 17025:2017','MIL-STD 45662A','ANSI/NCSL-Z540','AMS2750','ASTM E220','ISO/IEC Guide 25','ASTM E207','BAC5621','ANSI MC 96.1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermocouple wire and cable manufacturing", "Specialty wire and cable manufacturing", "Custom cable assembly", "Wire assembly", "Box build services", "Temperature calibration (NIST traceable, -320\u00b0F to 2400\u00b0F)", "Insulation extrusion/braiding (PVC to CEFIR\u00ae ceramic fiber)", "Alloy processing (iron-based, nickel-based, copper)", "Compliance testing (BAC5621, AMS2750, ASTM E220, ANSI MC 96.1)"], "industries": ["Aerospace composites", "Industrial OEM", "Metallurgy (steel and aluminum)", "Medical", "Engine testing (aviation)", "Power generation", "Temperature measurement"], "materials": ["Iron-based alloys", "Nickel-based alloys", "Copper", "PVC insulation", "CEFIR\u00ae ceramic fiber braids", "High-temperature insulation materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World\u2019s largest manufacturer of thermocouple wire and extension cable", "In\u2011house NIST\u2011traceable calibration lab (ISO 9001:2015, ISO/IEC 17025:2017)", "Calibration verified against U.S., British, and Dutch national standards", "Meets aerospace specs including BAC5621, AMS2750, ASTM E220", "Short lead times and competitive pricing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1941 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Saddle Brook, New Jersey -> db", "Ownership: Marmon Wire & Cable/Berkshire Hathaway subsidiary -> /about-us", "Largest thermocouple wire manufacturer claim -> /", "Full line of thermocouple wire from iron/nickel alloys and copper -> /about-us", "Insulation materials PVC to CEFIR\u00ae