UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1956 in Shawnee, Kansas, TED Manufacturing Corporation has operated continuously as a designer and manufacturer of RF coaxial connectors. The company is based in Shawnee Mission, Kansas, where it runs an all-inclusive shop that handles machining, plating, heat treating, soft solder, glass seal firing, inspection, assembly, and shipping under one roof.

TED produces custom and standard RF connectors, including BNC, TNC, SMB, and Adapter series, as well as hermetically sealed parts and specialty connectors such as the 104 Series transponder antennas, helical cable removable connectors, fuel-system connectors, and blind self-centering connectors. The company maintains a library of over 11 connector families plus custom designs drawn from 70 years of experience, with roughly half of its shipped volume consisting of custom or modified parts. Engineering support is provided from concept through production.

The company serves aerospace and avionics programs with transponder antennas and hermetic feed-throughs; defense customers with MIL-DTL-38999, BNC, TNC, and N connectors built in ITAR-registered cells; broadcast and telecom operators with tower-rated and weather-sealed cable assemblies, helical assemblies, and 75Ω BNC for SDI video; test and measurement labs with precision connectors through 40 GHz including 3.5 mm, 2.92 mm, and ATE-grade SMA; and industrial and energy sectors with ruggedized connectors for fuel systems.

TED emphasizes that keeping every manufacturing step in-house eliminates lost parts, miscommunication, and overlapping lead times, while using solely USA-sourced materials and components. The company cites restructured pricing and shorter-than-average lead times as key differentiators, and commits to responding to inquiries within one business day.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom RF connector design and manufacturing", "Standard RF connector series (BNC, TNC, SMB, Adapter)", "Hermetically sealed connector manufacturing", "Specialty connector manufacturing (104 Series transponder antennas, helical cable removable connectors, fuel system connectors, blind self-centering connectors)", "Precision machining", "Plating (silver, nickel, gold)", "Heat treating", "Soft soldering", "Glass seal firing", "Inspection and testing", "Assembly", "Engineering support (concept to production)", "Material traceability", "Assembly instruction documentation", "ITAR-compliant manufacturing", "Conflict minerals reporting"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Avionics", "Defense", "Broadcast & Telecom", "Test & Measurement", "Industrial & Energy"], "materials": ["Brass", "Silver plate", "Nickel", "Gold over Nickel", "Gold contact", "RG-58U", "RG-62", "RG-71/U", "RG-303/U", "Triax"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All manufacturing steps (machining, plating, heat treating, glass seal firing, inspection, assembly, shipping) under one roof", "USA-made materials and components exclusively", "Short to medium run custom RF connectors built to customer drawings and specifications", "Engineering support from concept through production", "ITAR-registered manufacturing with response within one business day"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1956 in Shawnee, Kansas -> db", "All-inclusive shop with machining, plating, heat treating, soft solder, glass seal firing, inspection, assembly, shipping under one roof -> /about", "USA-made materials and components -> /about", "70+ years building RF connectors -> /", "50% of shipped volume is custom or modified -> /", "11+ RF connector families in catalog plus custom designs -> /", "Industries served: Aerospace & Avionics, Defense, Broadcast & Telecom, Test & Measurement, Industrial & Energy -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ITAR -> db, /quality", "Team: Ted McGrade (President), Connor McGrade (General Manager), etc. -> /about", "Capabilities: custom RF connectors, standard RF series, hermetically sealed parts, specialty connectors -> /capabilities", "Products: BNC, TNC, SMB, Adapter series, 104 Series transponder antennas, helical cable removable connectors, fuel system connectors, blind self-centering connectors -> /", "Assembly instructions for various part series -> /quality", "Respond within 1 business day -> /capabilities", "Engineering support from concept through production -> /capabilities", "Short to medium run production -> /, /capabilities", "Hermetically sealed parts for pressure-sealed environments -> /capabilities", "Specialty connectors for requirements standard catalog parts cannot serve -> /capabilities", "Standard RF series stocked and built to industry/military standards -> /capabilities", "ITAR-registered manufacturing -> /", "MIL-DTL-38999, BNC, TNC, N connectors for defense -> /", "Tower-rated connectors, weather-sealed cable assemblies, helical assemblies, IP67-sealed tower-top terminations, 75\u03a9 BNC for SDI video -> /", "Lab-grade RF connectors through 40 GHz, 3.5mm, 2.92mm precision, ATE-grade high-cycle SMA -> /", "Ruggedized connectors for fuel systems -> /", "Materials: Brass, Silver plate, Nickel, Gold over Nickel, Gold contact, RG-58U, RG-62, RG-71/U, RG-303/U, Triax -> /quality", "Quality policy, ISO 9001 Certificate, Conflict Minerals Report -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "TED Manufacturing Corporation is a leading designer and manufacturer of RF type coaxial connectors.", "founded_year": "1956", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ted-manufacturing-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='TOA SE, Inc. operates from Nicholasville, Kentucky. The company traces its roots to 1956 when TOA Electronics Company was established in Nagoya, Japan. The U.S. subsidiary, TOA Electric USA, Inc., was founded in Lexington, Kentucky in 2001 to provide factory automation and systems integration for regional manufacturers. In 2007 the business moved to a new facility in Nicholasville and was renamed TOA SE (Systems Engineering); the legal name became TOA SE, Inc. in 2010.

The company designs and builds UL 508A‑certified control panels, provides on‑site programming, modifications and upgrades, and delivers turnkey machine design and build services. Its 27,000‑square‑foot project warehouse supports metal fabrication, post‑machining processing and NC tack‑up work.

TOA SE serves automotive and material‑handling manufacturers. Named customers include Toyota Material Handling, Toyota Motor Manufacturing, General Motors, Honda of America Manufacturing, Michigan Automotive Compressor and Toyotomi America Corporation.

