UPDATE companies SET description='TOMAR Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1969 in Chicago, Illinois, initially producing industrial warning equipment for heavy industry. The company is now headquartered in Gilbert, Arizona, and remains a family-owned and operated private business.

TOMAR designs and manufactures signaling, illumination, and control systems across five divisions: Automotive (visual and audible signaling, illumination, and optical preemption for mobile fleets including fire apparatus, police cruisers, and ambulances), Off-Road (LED light bars, illumination bars, and infrared systems for tactical and military use), Traffic (optical preemption and intersection control solutions for municipalities and traffic engineers), Industrial (strobes, sirens, beacons, and perimeter safety lighting for manufacturing, mining, warehousing, transportation hubs, and energy facilities), and Custom OEM (custom-engineered lighting and control systems, private-labeled devices, and ODM development for robotics, heavy equipment, and defense platforms). All products are engineered and assembled at the company''s Gilbert facility, which houses a 100-foot automated photometric light tunnel, goniometer, spectroradiometer, Faraday cage for EMI/EMC testing, environmental chambers, and a full in-house test lab.

The company serves plant managers, first responders, fleet operators, and public safety professionals worldwide. Its customer base spans emergency services, municipal government, traffic engineering, industrial manufacturing, mining, energy, military and defense, off-road vehicle operators, marine, robotics, and heavy equipment OEMs.

TOMAR emphasizes its ISO 9001:2015 certification, 100% burn-in testing, statistical process control, and warranties as quality differentiators. Since 2009 it has operated as an SRP Energy Star-rated manufacturer, powered by a 100 kW rooftop solar array, and pursues climate-conscious operations including energy load shifting and robust recycling.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom OEM/ODM product development", "Design and engineering (circuit simulation, firmware/software management, 3D CAD modeling, thermal simulation)", "In-house photometric testing (100-ft automated light tunnel, goniometer, spectroradiometer)", "EMI/EMC compliance testing (Faraday cage)", "Environmental stress testing (thermal chambers)", "Statistical Process Control (SPC)", "100% fixture burn-in testing", "Manufacturing and assembly in Gilbert, Arizona", "Private labeling", "Optical preemption and intersection control systems", "LED light bar and infrared system manufacturing", "Strobe, siren, beacon, and perimeter safety lighting production"], "industries": ["Emergency services", "Law enforcement", "Fire protection", "Emergency medical services", "Municipal government", "Traffic engineering", "Industrial manufacturing", "Mining", "Warehousing and logistics", "Transportation", "Energy and utilities", "Military and defense", "Off-road vehicles", "Marine", "Robotics", "Heavy equipment", "Custom OEM"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["100-ft automated photometric light tunnel", "High-precision goniometer", "Spectroradiometers", "Faraday cage instrumentation", "Environmental chambers", "Thermal simulation software", "3D CAD modeling software", "100 kW grid-tied solar power system", "SRP Energy Management System"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified with 100% burn-in testing", "In-house 100-ft photometric light tunnel aligned to FAA, SAE, and IES standards", "SRP Energy Star-rated manufacturer since 20