UPDATE companies SET description='United Electronic Industries (UEI) was founded in 1990 in Norwood, Massachusetts. The company began with ISA bus data acquisition boards and expanded to PCI and PXI boards in the mid-1990s.

UEI designs and manufactures PC/Ethernet data acquisition (DAQ) and control systems, data loggers/recorders, programmable automation controllers (PACs), and Modbus TCP solutions. The product line includes over 90 I/O boards covering analog input/output, digital I/O, serial/CAN, counter/timer, avionics, simulation, and power supply functions. All hardware is developed and manufactured in the United States.

UEI serves industries including nuclear energy, commercial and military aviation, space, oil and gas, commercial and military automotive, ship/submarine, energy/utilities, rail/transportation, and scientific research. Applications span hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) testing, health and usage monitoring (HUMS), engine test, VISTAS ED-247, iDDS, simulators/trainers, cybersecurity, embedded control and logging, automated test, and distributed DAQ and control.

UEI states that its products are developed and manufactured entirely in the U.S., and it participates in the E-Verify program. Supported programming environments include C/C++, LabVIEW, MATLAB, Simulink, C#, Python, .NET, VB.NET, and LabWindows/CVI.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Data acquisition and control", "Test and simulation", "Rugged I/O systems", "Industrial SCADA", "Measurement and logging", "Health monitoring", "Hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) testing", "Health and usage monitoring (HUMS)", "Engine test", "VISTAS ED-247 compliance", "iDDS implementation", "Simulator and trainer systems", "Cybersecurity solutions", "Embedded control and logging", "Automated test", "Distributed DAQ and control", "Calibration services (ISO/IEC 17025:2017)", "Training and enhanced support services"], "industries": ["Nuclear energy", "Commercial aviation", "Military aviation", "Space", "Oil and gas", "Commercial automotive", "Military automotive", "Ship and submarine", "Energy and utility", "Rail and transportation", "Scientific research"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1990 -> db", "Headquarters in Norwood, Massachusetts -> db", "First products were ISA bus DAQ boards -> description", "PCI and PXI boards added in mid-1990s -> description", "Over 90 I/O boards available -> homepage (/) ", "All products developed and manufactured in the United States -> homepage (/) ", "Five-year standard warranty on all hardware -> homepage (/) ", "Calibration certified to ISO/IEC 17025:2017 -> homepage (/) ", "Industries served: nuclear energy, commercial aviation, military aviation, space, oil & gas, commercial automotive, military automotive, ship/submarine, energy/utility, rail/transportation, scientific research -> homepage (/) ", "Applications: HIL, HUMS, engine test, VISTAS ED-247, iDDS, simulators/trainers, cybersecurity, embedded control & logging, automated t