UPDATE companies SET description='United Tool & Mold Inc. was founded in 1995 in Liberty, South Carolina, with a second strategic location in Rainbow City, Alabama. The company was established on the principle of "Keeping the Plastics Industry Running" to serve as a one-stop shop for mold-servicing needs, focusing on reducing customer downtime through rapid response and comprehensive repair capabilities.

The company provides repair and engineering change services for plastic injection and blow molds, operating a 60,000-square-foot facility in Liberty. Its capabilities include laser welding, large precision machining, massive mold fitting presses, and an 80" x 40" x 40" fluidized bed for cleaning mold components and hot runners. United Tool & Mold also offers on-site service with fully stocked vans for in-press repairs, preventive maintenance, and 24-hour emergency response. Engineering changes are performed using CAD platforms such as CATIA V4, V5, and Unigraphics, and the company manages new tool build projects through domestic and global sources.

United Tool & Mold serves the plastic injection molding and blow molding industries. Its customer base includes automotive suppliers such as Draexlmaier, which has cited the company''s ability to complete most repairs within one or two days and provide reliable outside tool support.

The company differentiates itself through around-the-clock availability, on-site service that travels to the customer''s facility, and engineering change lead times described as better than the industry average. Its founding philosophy centers on treating mold service as a partnership: "When you buy a tool from us, you''re not purchasing a mold – you''re purchasing a plastic part. You''re buying our service."', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection mold repair", "Blow mold repair", "Engineering changes (design and modification)", "Preventive maintenance", "On-site in-press repair service", "Laser welding", "Fluidized bed cleaning (80\" x 40\" x 40\")", "Large precision machining", "Massive mold fitting presses", "Heavy lifting and trucking logistics", "New tool build design and project management", "Tool design and modification", "Part modification", "CAD/CAM: CATIA V4, CATIA V5, Unigraphics", "24-hour operations", "Emergency repair response", "Quick turnaround repairs", "Mold cleaning", "Mold sampling and part validation support"], "industries": ["Plastic injection molding", "Blow molding"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["80\" x 40\" x 40\" fluidized bed", "Massive mold fitting presses", "Laser welding equipment", "Large precision machining equipment", "Fully stocked on-site service vans", "Heavy trucking and lifting equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24-hour emergency service and around-the-clock availability", "On-site mold repair with fully stocked service vans", "80\" x 40\" x 40\" fluidized bed for mold component cleaning", "Engineering change lead times better than industry average", "Large precision machining and massive mold fitting presses"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1995 -> db", "Headquarters Liberty, SC and Rainbow City, AL -> db and /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "60,000 sq ft facility in Liberty -> /", "Services: mold repair, engineering changes, on-site service, laser welding, fluidized bed cleaning, large machining, fitting presses -> /", "Industries: plastic injection and blow molding -> /", "Customer example: Draexlmaier (Dennis Quinby quote) -> /", "24-hour operations and emergency response -> /", "CAD software: CATIA V4, V5, Unigraphics -> /", "Fluidized bed dimensions 80\" x 40\" x 40\" -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "United Tool & Mold Inc. is a global provider of engineering changes and repair services for the plastic injection and blow molding industries.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/united-tool/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='united-tool-mold-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='United Poly Systems was established in 2011 in Albuquerque, New Mexico, by founders Jim Massengale and Bert Bridges, who brought over 40 years of combined industry experience. The company began with two HDPE pipe production lines and expanded to four by 2013. A second state-of-the-art manufacturing facility opened in Albuquerque in 2015, and four additional lines were added across both plants over the following four years. In June 2022, Atkore, Inc. (founded 1959, based in Harvey, IL) acquired United Poly Systems, and the business has since been acquired by Infra Pipe Solutions.

The company manufactures high- and medium-density polyethylene (HDPE/MDPE) pipe and conduit in diameters from 3/4-in. to 26-in. IPS, 4-in. to 24-in. DIPS, and 3/4-in. to 2-in. CTS. Operations span multiple plants across Allendale, SC; Thomasville, GA; Springfield, MO; Albuquerque, NM; Lovelady, TX; Dallas, TX; and Woodburn, OR. In its first decade, United Poly Systems produced over 120,000 miles of pipe. The manufacturing process includes resin quality inspections (cleanliness, carbon black content, melt flow index, density), dimensional testing (diameter, wall thickness, eccentricity, ovality, out-of-round), and tensile property testing (elongation at break, ring tensile burst, quick burst). Products are available in 12 colors with custom striping, packaged in reels, sticks, or coils, and can be customized with ribbed interiors, pull tape, or lubricated interiors.

United Poly Systems serves the broadband and telecommunications, power and communications, oil and gas, and energy utility markets. Customers include telecommunications contractors, broadband providers such as Foothills Broadband, utility district contractors, and electrical/high-voltage infrastructure projects. The company’s product suites — Comm-Line™, MicroPath™, Power-Line™, Pro-Line™, Sleeve-It!™, Hard-Line™, and Cable-in-Conduit — are designed for communications conduit, microduct, electrical conduit, large-diameter PVC replacement, and cable-in-conduit applications.

The company emphasizes its agile business model, coast-to-coast manufacturing footprint that reduces freight costs and lead times, and compliance with the Buy American Act for domestic sourcing. Its quality program covers resin, dimensional, and burst testing to UL, NSF, AWWA, and ASTM standards.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed','NSF certified','AWWA compliant','ASTM standards for plastic pipe','Buy American Act compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HDPE pipe extrusion", "Custom pipe manufacturing", "Resin quality inspection (cleanliness, carbon black content, melt flow index, density)", "Dimensional quality testing (diameter, wall thickness, eccentricity, ovality, out-of-round)", "Tensile property testing (elongation at break, ring tensile burst, quick burst)", "Custom striping and coloring (12 colors)", "Packaging in reels, sticks, and coils", "Ribbed interior extrusion", "Pull tape installation", "Lubricated interior coating"], "industries": ["Broadband and telecommunications", "Power and communications", "Oil and gas", "Energy utilities", "Electrical and high voltage infrastructure"], "materials": ["HDPE (High Density Polyethylene)", "MDPE (Medium Density Polyethylene)", "Polyethylene"], "equipment": ["HDPE extrusion production lines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Coast-to-coast manufacturing locations reducing freight costs and lead times", "Agile business model meeting customer needs without large-producer overhead", "Comprehensive in-house quality testing: resin, dimensional, tensile, and burst", "Buy American Act compliant domestic sourcing", "Fully customizable HDPE pipe: diameter, thickness, color, striping, ribbed interior, pull tape, lubricated interior"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2011 by Jim Massengale and Bert Bridges -> /about-us", "Two production lines in 2011, four by 2013, second facility Albuquerque 2015, four more lines added -> /about-us", "Over 120,000 miles pipe produced in first decade -> /about-us", "Acquired by Atkore June 2022 -> /about-us", "Manufacturing locations across 7 states -> /", "HDPE pipe diameters 3/4-in. to 26-in. IPS, 4-in. to 24-in. DIPS, 3/4-in. to 2-in. CTS -> /about-us", "Resin, dimensional, tensile quality testing details -> /", "12 colors, custom striping, reels/sticks/coils, ribbed interior, pull tape, lubricated interior -> /about-us", "Markets: broadband/telecom, power/communications, oil & gas, energy -> /", "Product suites: Comm-Line, MicroPath, Power-Line, Pro-Line, Sleeve-It!, Hard-Line, Cable-in-Conduit -> /", "Certifications: UL Listed, NSF, AWWA, ASTM, Buy American Act -> /", "Materials: HDPE, MDPE, polyethylene -> /", "Minimum order length based on diameter -> /", "Headquarters Albuquerque, NM -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we manufacture high and medium density conduit and pressure polyethylene pipe", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Minimum order length based on pipe diameter; consult Minimum Order Quantities guide", "export_compliance": ["Buy American Act compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='united-poly-systems' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Universal Plastic Mold (UPM) is a family-owned custom plastic injection molder founded in 1962 in Baldwin Park, California. The company has operated continuously under family ownership, with second-generation leadership in place since 2007.

UPM operates 30 injection molding machines ranging from 150 to 2,000 tons, including five presses at 1,500+ tons and three at 2,000 tons, in a single ~130,000 sq ft facility. The company provides full turnkey scope — molding, finishing (painting, silk-screening, hot-stamping), complex assembly, PCB integration, kitting, packaging, and distribution — under one ISO 9001:2015 quality system. Approximately 300 employees and $30M+ annual revenue.

UPM serves mid-market OEMs in automotive, specialty vehicles, industrial, high-end electronics, medical and laboratory equipment, and packaging, with selective consumer goods and hardware work. Customers include OEMs running hard-tooled production programs with minimum economic runs of 500 pieces per release through annual volumes in the millions.

The company emphasizes single point of accountability — the Account Manager and Program Manager are the same person — a 24-hour email reply standard, and published performance metrics (99.33% on-time delivery, 5.4 DPMO, 98% customer retention). Domestic production keeps customer-owned tooling under U.S. jurisdiction, and first-pass DFM is provided at no additional cost.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Injection Molding", "Large Part & High Tonnage Molding", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Mold Flow Analysis", "Tooling and Fabrication", "Assembly Services", "PCB Integration", "Kitting", "Packaging", "Distribution", "Painting", "Silk-screening", "Hot-stamping", "PPAP Level 3", "First Article Inspection (FAI)", "Lot-level Traceability", "Finishing", "Turnkey Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Specialty Vehicles", "Industrial", "High-End Electronics", "Medical and Laboratory Equipment", "Packaging", "Consumer Goods", "Hardware"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["30 injection molding machines (150\u20132,000 ton)", "5 presses at 1,500+ tons", "3 presses at 2,000 tons"], "volume": "500 pieces per release to millions annually", "lead_time": "2\u20133 weeks post-tooling", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single point of program ownership: Account Manager and Program Manager are the same person", "24-hour email reply standard with live phone answer during business hours", "Published performance: 99.33% on-time delivery, 5.4 DPMO, 98% customer retention (12-month rolling averages)", "Full turnkey scope under one ISO 9001:2015 quality system \u2014 molding, finishing, assembly, PCB integration, kitting, packaging, distribution", "West Coast large-tonnage capacity: 30 machines 150\u20132,000 tons including 5 at 1,500+ tons and 3 at 2,000 tons"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1962 in Baldwin Park, California -> /about", "Family-owned with second-generation leadership since 2007 -> /about", "30 injection 