UPDATE companies SET description='Vesper Medical, Inc. is a privately held medical device company based in Radnor, Pennsylvania. The company was formed in 2016 by Bruce J. Shook as a spinout of Intact Vascular, following Intact Vascular''s acquisition by Royal Philips in 2020. Shook, a veteran medical device executive with over 30 years of experience, previously co-founded Neuronetics and served as president of Abiomed.

Vesper Medical develops a next-generation, modular venous stent portfolio designed to treat deep venous disease, specifically addressing anatomical challenges in the iliac and femoral veins. The platform allows physicians to customize therapy for a broad range of patient needs.

Its scientific advisory board includes clinicians from institutions such as Christiana Care Health Services, St. Francis Hospital, Stanford University, and the University of Pennsylvania. Investors include New Enterprise Associates, Gilde Healthcare, Vensana Capital, and Quaker Partners.

