UPDATE companies SET description='Vital Systems Corporation was founded in 1986 in Reno, Nevada, the same year it earned Department of Defense certification to manufacture electronics for military applications.

The shop specializes in printed circuit board assembly, box builds, and engineering support, with a focus on surface-mount technology that includes 01005 passives, BGA, QFN, and package-on-package placement. It runs both wave and nitrogen-assisted selective soldering, backed by automated optical inspection, X-ray inspection, and statistical process control.

Its customer base spans aerospace and defense primes — U.S. Navy, U.S. Air Force, Lockheed Martin, Boeing, Raytheon — as well as industrial OEMs in the post-production studio equipment sector and automotive safety systems such as Tesla. The company also serves harsh-environment controls for energy and heavy machinery.

Vital Systems differentiates itself through an IPC-A-610 Class 3 mindset applied to every build, targeting 99 percent untested first-pass yield and 100 percent tested first-pass yield. It has offered RoHS-compliant soldering since 2004 and provides consigned and onsite inventory management with real-time MRP visibility. Customer relationships average 25 years, with one account dating back to 1988.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','DOD Certification (defense electronics manufacturing)','US Navy Highest Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (SMT)", "Box Build Assembly", "Engineering Design Services", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole Wave Soldering", "Selective Soldering (Nitrogen)", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "X-Ray Inspection", "Statistical Process Control (SPC) Monitoring", "RoHS-Compliant Soldering", "Turnkey Supply Chain Management", "Consigned Inventory Management", "Onsite Inventory Management with MRP", "Prototype Assembly (1-day expedited, 5-day standard)", "Production Assembly (10-day standard)", "Small Form Factor PCBA (0.25\" x 0.25\")", "BGA/QFN/POP/01005 Placement", "IPC-A-610 Class 3 Manufacturing", "Electrical Test & Programming", "Component Programming & Test"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Automotive Safety Systems", "Industrial & Energy (Harsh-Environment Controls)", "Post-Production / Studio Equipment", "Military Electronics"], "materials": ["RoHS-compliant lead-free solder alloys", "Surface mount components (BGA, QFN, 01005, POP)", "Through-hole components"], "equipment": ["Sophisticated robotics for SMT placement", "Wave soldering equipment", "Selective soldering with nitrogen gas", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) systems", "X-Ray inspection systems", "Statistical Process Control (SPC) monitoring", "ERP/MRP system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Prototype: 1 day (expedited) or 5 days (standard); Production: 10 business days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["99% untested f