UPDATE companies SET description='WCJ Pilgrim Wire was founded in 1998 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, by William Jones, who remains the company’s president. Initially focused on supplying high‑quality stitching wire to the graphic arts industry, the business expanded over the years to serve industrial, baling, brush, packaging and automotive markets. In 2017 the company partnered with DDD Group and opened its first dedicated manufacturing facility in York, Pennsylvania, where it continues to produce wire products using domestic steel.

The company manufactures a broad range of wire products including coated and electro‑plated wire, industrial wire, spring and music wire, brush and broom staple wire, flat wire, stitching wire and custom wire solutions. Its capabilities cover custom base materials, plating types (copper, zinc, tin, nickel, polymer), tensile requirements, diameters and packaging.

WCJ Pilgrim serves customers in industrial manufacturing, graphic arts and publishing, waste disposal and recycling, medical device production, brush and broom manufacturing, HVAC ducting, food processing and transportation. The company also supplies baling wire for packaging and box‑binding applications and provides wire for automotive components.

The founder’s stated mission is to make the highest quality wire using the latest state‑of‑the‑art machines and components in America.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire manufacturing", "Electroplating (copper, zinc, tin, nickel, polymer)", "Electroshield\u2122 electroplating process", "Wire drawing (hard drawn, annealed)", "Spring and music wire manufacturing", "Flat wire manufacturing", "Stitching wire manufacturing", "Brush and broom staple wire manufacturing", "Wire spooling and de\u2011spooling equipment", "Spiral binding wire production", "Baling wire production", "Coating and plating services"], "industries": ["Industrial manufacturing", "Graphic arts and publishing", "Waste disposal and recycling", "Medical devices", "Brush and broom manufacturing", "HVAC ducting", "Food processing", "Transportation", "Packaging", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Low-carbon steel", "High-carbon steel (C1045-C1080)", "Copper", "Zinc (galvanized)", "Tin", "Nickel", "Polymer coatings", "Brass", "Bronze", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Electroshield\u2122 electroplating line", "Wire spooling and de\u2011spooling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 in Milwaukee, Wisconsin -> db, /about", "Founder William Jones, current President -> /about", "Partnership with DDD Group in 2017, opened York PA facility -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> homepage, db", "Product lines: coated/plated, industrial, spring/music, brush/staple, flat, stitching, custom -> homepage, /about", "Electroshield\u2122 eco-friendly electroplating process -> homepage", "Industries served: Industrial, Graphic Arts, Waste Disposal, Medical, Brush & Broom, Ducting, Food, Transportation -> homepage, /about", "Team members listed (William Jones, Kris Shaw, Mark Hurt, etc.) -> /about", "Mission: highest quality wire using latest state-of-the-art machines and components in Amer