UPDATE companies SET description='Wald Wire & Manufacturing Co. was founded in 1951 in Oshkosh, Wisconsin, as a small wire-forming shop serving small and midsize manufacturers in the Northeast Wisconsin region. The company remains headquartered in Oshkosh and has grown from a 9,000-square-foot facility with a handful of employees to a multi-shop operation.

Today the company operates over 200,000 square feet across three shops and employs more than 100 people. The wire-forming robotics produce items such as shelving, racks, baskets, fan guards, and pegboards in a wide range of metal materials.

Wald Wire serves both small-to-midsize manufacturers and Fortune 500 companies, offering no quantity minimums, fast turnarounds, and immediate shipping for short or long production runs. Customers rely on the shop for individual components, full assemblies, and end-to-end fulfillment.

The company emphasizes a “flexible, fully-integrated supply chain partner” model, promising “unbending results” through a relentless commitment to delivering quality welding, wire, tube, and sheet metal fabrication within the promised timeline.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC 3D wire forming", "CNC 2D wire forming", "Wire forming", "Spot welding", "Stamping", "Finishing", "In-house toolmaking", "Rolled threads", "Cut threads", "Tube fabrication", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Laser cutting", "Forming", "Rolling", "Welding", "Custom wire forming", "Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Assembly", "End-to-end fulfillment"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Metal"], "equipment": ["Custom wire forming robotics", "CNC 3D wire forming machines", "CNC 2D wire forming machines", "Laser cutting equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No quantity minimums on any order", "Fast turnarounds and immediate shipping for short runs", "Over 200,000 sq ft across three shops with in-house toolmaking", "Serves both small manufacturers and Fortune 500 companies", "75+ years of wire forming and fabrication experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1951 in Oshkosh, Wisconsin -> /about", "Started as small wire forming shop for small to midsize manufacturers -> /about", "Expanded from 9,000 sq ft to over 200,000 sq ft across three shops -> /about", "Employs over 100 people -> /about", "Services: wire forming, welding, tube and sheet metal fabrication -> /about", "CNC 2D and 3D wire forming -> /about", "Wire forming robotics produce shelving, racks, baskets, fan guards, pegboards -> /", "No quantity minimums -> /", "Fast turnarounds, short runs, immediate shipping -> /", "Serves small to midsize manufacturers and Fortune 500 companies -> /about", "ISO9001 certification -> db", "In-house toolmaking, spot welding, stamping, rolled threads, cut threads -> /", "Laser cutting, forming, rolling -> /about", "Custom wire forming, custom sheet metal fabrication -> /", "Full assemblies, end-to-end fulfillment -> /about", "Headquarters Oshkosh, Wisconsin -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our manufacturing facility, tools and knowledge in welding, laser cutting, forming, rolling and more will meet your customers'' tube and sheet metal fabrication needs.", "founded_year": "1951", "employee_count": "over 100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wald-wire-manufacturing-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1977 in Dallas, Texas, Wallace Electronics is a woman-owned manufacturer of custom cable assemblies and electronic enclosures. The company has served the electronics industry for over four decades from its facility on Miller Road.

The company designs and manufactures custom cable assemblies, wiring harnesses, and electronic enclosures. Its capabilities include custom fabrication, in-house overmolding, custom shielding and pinout design, reverse engineering from samples, and engineering support from prototype through scaled production. Wallace works with wire gauges from 30 AWG to 2/0 using materials such as PVC, silicone, and Teflon, and maintains over 300 applicators for precision terminations. The facility also provides continuity testing, pull tests, electrical validation, and environmental testing for vibration and temperature extremes.

Wallace serves a broad range of industries, including industrial automation, military, medical, automotive, aerospace, transportation (bus and rail), renewable energy (solar and wind), telecommunications, security, oil and gas, and food and beverage. Its customers are primarily OEMs and contract manufacturers that require custom cable solutions for specialized equipment and harsh environments.

The company emphasizes flexibility and partnership, offering connector-agnostic designs, design-for-manufacturability consulting, stocking programs, drop-shipping, and blanket orders to simplify supply chains. Quality is backed by ISO 9001:2015 certification, UL approval for wiring harnesses, and compliance with RoHS, REACH, DFARS/ITAR, and conflict minerals requirements. As a woman-owned business, Wallace highlights diversity and leadership in manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC/WHMA-A-620','RoHS','UL','CSA','DFARS/ITAR','REACH','Conflict Minerals']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly manufacturing", "Wiring harness manufacturing", "Electronic enclosure manufacturing", "Custom overmolding", "Custom shielding and pinout design", "Reverse engineering from samples", "Engineering support and design for manufacturability", "Prototyping", "Expedited production and shipping", "Continuity testing", "Pull testing", "Electrical validation", "Environmental testing (vibration, temperature extremes)", "Compliance documentation", "Kitting", "Stocking programs", "Drop-shipping", "Blanket orders", "Inventory planning", "Connector-agnostic designs", "Custom labeling and color coding"], "industries": ["Industrial Automation", "Military", "Medical", "Automotive", "Lawn and Garden", "HVAC", "Lighting", "Telecommunications", "Gaming", "Security", "Solar", "Wind", "Satellite Communications", "Oil and Gas", "Food and Beverage", "Aerospace", "Transportation (Bus and Rail)", "Renewable Energy"], "materials": ["PVC", "silicone", "Teflon (PTFE)", "copper"], "equipment": ["300+ applicators for precision terminations"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Prototypes often ship within 1-2 weeks; expedited shipping available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house overmolding for custom connectors", "Over 300 applicators for precision terminations", "Prototypes ship within 1-2 weeks", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with UL-approved wiring harnesses", "Woman-owned business with DFARS/ITAR compliance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 in Dallas, Texas -> db", "Woman-owned manufacturer -> db, /, /about", "Custom cable assemblies, wiring harnesses, electronic enclosures -> /, /about", "In-house overmolding, custom shielding, pinouts -> /", "Over 300 applicators for precision terminations -> /", "Prototypes ship within 1-2 weeks -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /quality", "UL-approved wiring harnesses -> /, /quality", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 -> /quality", "RoHS, REACH, Conflict Minerals compliance -> /, /quality", "DFARS/ITAR compliant -> /quality", "Cage Code 4T656 -> /quality", "Industries served: Industrial Automation, Military, Medical, Automotive, Lawn and Garden, HVAC, Lighting, Telecom, Gaming, Security, Solar, Wind, Sat Com, Oil and Gas, Food and Beverage -> /", "Also serves Aerospace, Medical Devices, Transportation (Bus & Rail), Renewable Energy -> /", "Materials: PVC, silicone, Teflon, wire gauges 30 AWG to 2/0 -> /", "Engineering support, design for manufacturability -> /", "Stocking programs, drop-shipping, blanket orders -> /", "Continuity testing, pull tests, electrical validation, environmental testing -> /", "Connector-agnostic designs, custom labeling and color coding -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wallace Electronics is a Woman Owned Manufacturer of Custom Cable Assemblies and Electronic Enclosures.", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "4T656", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["DFARS/ITAR", "RoHS", "REACH", "Conflict Minerals"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/wallace-electronics-inc/"], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wallace-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Warrenton Steel is a veteran-owned steel supplier and fabricator based in Warrenton, Missouri. Founded in 1989, the company has served business partners across the region for over three decades.

The company stocks a broad range of carbon and structural steel products—including merchant bar, structural shapes, pipe, tube, plate, and metal building panels—and provides value-added services such as water jet cutting and mobile welding. Its inventory includes shims, flat bar, base plates, and welding practice coupons, supported by an extensive in-stock inventory and local pickup options.

Warrenton Steel serves construction, petrochemical, aerospace, power generation, and transportation industries. Its materials meet specifications for commercial buildings, petrochemical plants, aerospace components (AS 9100D certified), power plants, renewable energy infrastructure, bridges, and railways.

