UPDATE companies SET description='Washington Metal Fabricators operates from Washington, Missouri, about 50 miles southwest of St. Louis. The company was founded in 1979 and has served as a manufacturing cornerstone in the region for over four decades.

The firm positions itself as an engineering-focused partner rather than a conventional job shop, specializing in optimizing manufacturing processes for clients. Its 154,000-square-foot campus includes a 50,000-square-foot assembly and distribution center. Equipment spans tube and sheet laser cutting (four Trumpf lasers, Trumpf 7000 tube laser), CNC punching, nine brake presses (38–175 tons), three coil-fed stamping lines, three rolling centers, 15 welding stations (manual and robotic, including a Genesis Versa2), 15 grinding stations, and a Nordson powder-coat line with custom finishes such as wood grain and corten. Services range from product consulting, 2D/3D CAD, and prototyping through fabrication, welding, finishing, assembly, and warehousing, supporting both prototype and high-volume runs.

The company serves customers from small local shops to Fortune 500 manufacturers across sectors including electrical enclosures, machine components, power-grid transformer tanks, OEM components, and HVAC products. It also collaborates with its sister company, EZ Fabricating, to incorporate non-metal materials and provide inventory management.

Washington Metal Fabricators was built on the principle that diverse equipment investment enables the most efficient manufacturing route for each part. By reviewing every aspect of a client’s design, the firm aims to deliver precision, speed to market, and competitive pricing without designing the product itself.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product consulting and engineering", "2D CAD / 3D solid modeling (AutoCAD, Autodesk Inventor)", "Instruction and parts book writing", "FTP drawing transfer", "Tube laser cutting (up to 8 in. diameter, 3/8 in. wall)", "Sheet laser cutting (up to 5 ft \u00d7 10 ft, carbon steel 5/8 in., stainless 1/2 in., aluminum 1/4 in.)", "CNC turret punching (carbon steel up to 1/4 in.)", "Metal forming / brake pressing (38\u2013175 tons, up to 12 ft length)", "Metal stamping (coil-fed lines, 30\u2013150 tons)", "Metal rolling (up to 10-gauge steel, 72 in. length)", "Manual welding (MIG, TIG, resistance, AWS D1.1)", "Robotic welding (Genesis Versa2, 5 ft \u00d7 10 ft fixtures)", "Spot welding (15\u2013200 KVA)", "Grinding and polishing (Timesavers, tube polishing)", "Powder coating (Nordson line, four-stage phosphate wash, custom finishes)", "Assembly and warehousing", "Prototyping", "Reverse engineering", "OEM component manufacturing", "Electrical enclosure fabrication", "HVAC product fabrication", "Conveyor line production"], "industries": ["Electrical enclosures", "Machine components", "Power grid / transformer tanks", "OEM components", "HVAC products"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Steel tubing (round, square, rectangular, oval)", "Structural steel"], "equipment": ["Trumpf 7000 Tube Laser", "Trumpf sheet lasers (4 units)", "Turret punching centers (3 units)", "Brake presses (9 units, 38\u2013175 tons)", "Coil-fed stamping lines (3 units)", "Stamping presses (7 units, 30\u2013150 tons)", "Rolling centers (3 units)", "Welding stations (15 units, MIG/TIG/resistance)", "Genesis Versa2 robotic welder", "Spot welders (15\u2013200 KVA)", "Grinding stations (15 units, Timesavers, tube polishers)", "Nordson Powder Coat Line (four-stage phosphate wash)"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineering-first approach: optimizes manufacturing processes rather than simply executing prints", "Broad equipment portfolio (laser, punch, press, stamp, roll, weld, finish) under one roof", "Combined capabilities with sister company EZ Fabricating for non-metal materials and supply-chain services", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "Custom powder-coat finishes including realistic wood grain, marble stone, and corten"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 -> /about", "Headquarters Washington, Missouri (50 miles SW of St. Louis) -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about, /services", "154,000 sq. ft. facility with 50,000 sq. ft. assembly/distribution center -> /about", "Sister company EZ Fabricating -> /about, /", "Engineering services: consulting, prototyping, 2D/3D CAD (AutoCAD, Inventor) -> /, /about", "Tube laser cutting: Trumpf 7000, up to 8 in. dia, 3/8 in. wall -> /", "Sheet laser cutting: four Trumpf lasers, 5''x10'', carbon steel 5/8\", stainless 1/2\", aluminum 1/4\" -> /", "CNC punching: three turret centers, carbon steel up to 1/4\" -> /", "Metal forming: nine brake presses 38-175 tons, up to 12 ft -> /", "Metal stamping: three coil-fed lines, seven presses 30-150 tons -> /", "Metal rolling: three centers, up to 10-gauge, 72 in. -> /", "Manual & robotic welding: 15 stations, MIG/TIG/resistance, AWS D1.1, Genesis Versa2, spot welders 15-200 KVA -> /", "Grinding/polishing: 15 stations, Timesavers, tube polishing -> /", "Powder coating: Nordson line, four-stage phosphate, custom finishes (wood grain, marble, corten) -> /", "Assembly & warehousing -> /, /about", "Industries: electrical enclosures, machine components, power grid tanks, OEM components, HVAC products -> /,