UPDATE companies SET description='Wells Vehicle Electronics is headquartered in Fond du Lac, Wisconsin, with a 200,000-square-foot distribution and logistics center in Centerville, Iowa. The company was founded in 1903 by Robert Wells to supply electrical components to the nascent automobile industry, working alongside early innovators such as Henry Ford. The current Fond du Lac facility was constructed in 1983 and expanded in 1995, 1997, and 2013, while the Centerville complex has operated since 1986.

Wells designs, engineers, and manufactures a broad line of automotive electrical components, including ignition parts, emissions components, switches, sensors, regulators, solenoids, and relays. The Centerville distribution center runs proprietary packaging lines, automated order picking and stocking, and real-time inventory control across more than 33,000 active part numbers. The company also provides technical support staffed by certified technicians.

The company serves original equipment manufacturers, professional repair shops, warehouse distributors, and do-it-yourself customers across North America, South America, Europe, Asia, and Australia. Wells has been a member of the Automotive Warehouse Distributors Association since 1947, reflecting its deep roots in the aftermarket supply chain.

Wells states its mission is to create innovative win-win solutions for associates and business partners in vehicle electronics, with a vision to be a dominant global solutions provider offering a broad selection of products and customer service. The company emphasizes sustainable practices, holding ISO 14001:2015 certification and earning the 2004 Iowa Recycling Award for Excellence at its Centerville facility.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automotive electronics manufacturing", "Ignition component production", "Emissions component production", "Switch manufacturing", "Sensor manufacturing", "Regulator and solenoid production", "Relay manufacturing", "Product distribution and logistics", "Automated order picking and stocking", "Real-time inventory control", "Proprietary packaging", "Technical support", "Engineering and product development"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Original equipment manufacturers (OEM)", "Vehicle repair professionals", "Do-it-yourself (DIY) automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Proprietary packaging lines", "Automated order picking/stocking systems", "Real-time inventory control system", "Product-management system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 14001:2015 certified environmental management system", "200,000 sq. ft. distribution complex with proprietary packaging lines and automated order picking/stocking", "Real-time inventory control and product-management system with 33,000+ active item numbers", "Certified technicians providing expert technical support via dedicated hotline", "Member of Automotive Warehouse Distributors Association since 1947"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1903 by Robert Wells -> /about", "Headquarters Fond du Lac, WI -> /about", "Distribution center Centerville, IA 200,000 sq ft since 1986 -> /about", "ISO 14001:2015 certification -> /about", "33,000+ active item numbers -> /about", "Product categories: ignition, emissions, switches, sensors, regulators, solenoids, relays -> /", "Industries: OEMs, repair professionals, DIYers -> /", "Member of Automotive Warehouse Distributors Association since 1947 -> /about", "Facility built 1983, additions 1995, 1997, new building 2013 -> /about", "Leadership team names -> /about", "Mission and vision statements -> /about", "Technical support hotline with certified technicians -> /", "Omega Holdings acquisition 2026 -> /", "Iowa Recycling Award 2004 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "For more than 120 years, Wells has been a leader and innovator in automotive electrical components for OEMs, repair professionals and do-it-yourselfers alike.", "founded_year": "1903", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wells-vehicle-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Widener Metals, Inc. operates from Fallsington, Pennsylvania, and has served Southeastern Pennsylvania and New Jersey since 2013. The business is locally owned, family-owned, and veteran-owned.

The company stocks a range of metals including structural steel, aluminum, stainless steel, and expanded metal in forms such as I-beams, tubing, and perforated sheet. It adds value through saw cutting, plasma cutting, shearing, punching, bending, priming, and painting services. The shop offers same-day or next-day service and will cut material while customers wait.

Widener Metals emphasizes its 35-plus years of industry experience, veteran-owned status, and a commitment to customer satisfaction. It differentiates itself with no minimum order charges, same-day or next-day fulfillment, and in-store pickup and delivery options.', certifications=ARRAY['Veteran-owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Saw cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Shearing", "Punching", "Bending", "Priming", "Painting", "Hole punching"], "industries": ["Construction", "Manufacturing", "Transportation", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Structural Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless Steel", "Expanded Metal", "I Beams", "Perforated Sheet Metal", "Rectangular Tubing", "Square Tubing"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day or next-day service", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day or next-day service", "No minimum order charge", "Cutting while you wait", "Veteran-owned and family-owned", "35+ years of industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2013 -> /about", "Headquarters Fallsington, Pennsylvania -> db", "Family-owned and veteran-owned -> /about, /", "Same-day or next-day service -> /", "No minimum order charge -> /", "Materials: Structural Steel, Aluminum, Stainless Steel, Expanded Metal -> /about", "Services: Saw cutting, Plasma cutting, Shearing, Punching, Bending, Priming, Painting -> /services", "Industries: Construction, Manufacturing, Transportation, Industrial -> /", "Language: English -> /about", "Veteran-owned certification -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Metal Distributor in Southeastern PA and NJ", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order charge", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='widener-metals-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wirthwein Fountain Inn, LLC operates in Fountain Inn, South Carolina. The facility was established in 2012 and operated as South Carolina Plastics, LLC until June 2020, when it became part of the Wirthwein Group, a family-owned business founded in 1949.

It produces weight-reduced plastic solutions for narrow assembly spaces, complex geometries and surfaces, maximum-security components for rail fastening systems, dimensionally stable and temperature-resistant parts from advanced thermoplastics, and economic plastic components for white goods, stoves, and floor-care devices.

The company serves the mobility, rail infrastructure, new energy, home appliance, medical, and interior design industries. The group’s global footprint spans 20 companies across Europe, Asia, and the United States.

Wirthwein emphasizes its family-owned independence as a source of dynamic decision-making and long-term customer partnerships. The group describes itself as a reliable, stable partner that cultivates lasting market relationships while delivering innovative mold solutions and global production strategies.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','IATF 16949','UL certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastics technology (Kunststofftechnik)", "Mold design and manufacturing", "Injection molding", "Assembly and logistics", "Weight-reduced plastic solutions", "Complex geometry and surface finishing", "Rail fastening system components", "Advanced thermoplastic component production", "White goods and appliance components"], "industries": ["Mobility", "Rail Infrastructure", "New Energy", "Home Appliance", "Medical", "Interior Design"], "materials": ["Advanced thermoplastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned independence and dynamic decision-making", "Global footprint with 20 sites in Europe, Asia, and the USA", "Certified to IATF 16949, ISO 9001, ISO 14001, and UL", "Specialist in innovative molds and weight-reduced plastic solutions", "Focus on long-term customer partnerships"], "facts_used": ["Location: Fountain Inn, South Carolina -> /", "Founded: 2012 (as Wirthwein Fountain Inn, LLC) -> /", "Former name: South Carolina Plastics, LLC until June 2020 -> /", "Group founded: 1949, family-owned -> db", "Group employees: 2,700+ across 20 companies in Europe, Asia, USA -> db", "Certifications: IATF 16949, ISO 9001, ISO 14001, UL certification -> /", "Competencies: Plastics technology (Kunststofftechnik) -> /", "Products: innovative molds, weight-reduced plastic solutions, complex geometries, rail fastening components, advanced thermoplastic parts, white goods components -> db", "Industries served: Mobility, Rail Infrastructure, New Energy, Home Appliance, Medical, Interior Design -> db", "Ownershi