UPDATE companies SET description='Yaskawa America''s Drives & Motion Division is headquartered in Santa Clara, California. The division operates as a wholly owned subsidiary of Yaskawa Electric Corporation of Japan, a company founded in 1915. The U.S. corporation was created to provide automation solutions and support to customers across North, Central, and South America.

The division manufactures medium‑voltage switchgear — including pad‑mounted gas‑insulated and gas rotary‑arc models — low‑voltage switchgear, variable frequency drives, motor controllers, electric motors, and robotics automation systems. It describes itself as the world’s largest manufacturer of AC inverter drives, servo and motion control, and robotics automation systems, and has produced quality products in North America for more than 40 years.

Products serve utilities, industrial manufacturing, data centers, and commercial buildings. They are sold through direct sales, partners, representatives, dealers, and distributors. The division also supports applications in packaging, processing, and general manufacturing, offering solutions such as data‑center cooling VFDs, the iC9200 machine controller, and the iQpump605 pump drive.

Yaskawa emphasizes a quality policy that places continual improvement and customer satisfaction at the forefront, stating it has set standards competitors strive to meet. The division’s founding purpose was to bring Japanese automation expertise to the Americas, backed by a parent company with over a century of experience in productivity‑improving automation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medium-voltage switchgear manufacturing", "Low-voltage switchgear manufacturing", "Variable frequency drive manufacturing", "Motor controller manufacturing", "Electric motor manufacturing", "Robotics automation systems integration", "AC inverter drive manufacturing", "Servo and motion control manufacturing", "Automation solutions engineering", "Technical training services", "CNC software development (Compass 2)", "Machine controller design (iC9200)", "Pump drive systems (iQpump605)", "Data center cooling VFD solutions"], "industries": ["Utilities", "Industrial manufacturing", "Data centers", "Commercial buildings"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s largest manufacturer of AC inverter drives, servo and motion control, and robotics automation systems", "Producing quality products in North America for 40+ years", "Wholly-owned subsidiary of Yaskawa Electric Corporation (Japan)", "Multi\u2011channel distribution: direct sales, partners, representatives, dealers, distributors", "Quality policy prioritizing continual improvement and customer satisfaction"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Santa Clara, California -> db", "Founded 1915 (parent company) -> db", "Wholly-owned subsidiary of Yaskawa Electric Corporation -> /about-us", "Created to provide automation solutions in Americas -> /about-us", "World''s largest manufacturer of AC inverter drives, servo, motion control, robotics -> /about-us", "Producing quality products in North America for 40+ years -> /about-us", "Products: medium-voltage switchgear, low-voltage switchgear, VFDs, motor controllers, electric motors, robotics -> db, /about-us", "Industries served: utilities, industrial manufacturing, data centers, commercial buildings -> db", "Sales channels: direct, partners, representatives, dealers, distributors -> /about-us", "Quality policy: continual improvement, customer satisfaction -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2008 certification -> db", "Product lines: GA501 AC Microdrive, iC9200 Controllers, Sigma-X, iQpump605, Compass 2, Motoman robotics -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Yaskawa is the world''s largest manufacturer of AC Inverter Drives, Servo and Motion Control, and Robotics Automation Systems.", "founded_year": "1915", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='yaskawa-america-drives-motion-division' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zentech Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Baltimore, Maryland, with additional facilities in Richardson, Texas, and Bloomington, Illinois. The company operates as an electronic manufacturing services (EMS) provider specializing in high-reliability, high-complexity assemblies for mission-critical applications.

The company delivers full-turnkey electronic manufacturing services, including printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), system-level assembly and integration, comprehensive inspection and testing, higher-level assembly (HLA), new product introduction (NPI), program management, test development, and supply chain services. Zentech operates 180,000 square feet of manufacturing space across three sites, equipped with 11 surface-mount technology (SMT) lines, and focuses on low-to-medium volume, high-mix production of complex, high-reliability assemblies compliant with IPC 610 Class 2 and Class 3 standards.

Zentech serves primarily the defense and aerospace sector, which accounts for approximately 85 percent of its business, along with medical device manufacturers (10 percent) and commercial/industrial clients (5 percent). Its assemblies are used in mission-critical applications that protect national infrastructure and warfighters, though specific customer names are not disclosed.

Zentech emphasizes its comprehensive certification portfolio—including AS9100, ISO 13485, ITAR registration, IPC 610 Source Supplier, IPC J-STD-001 Space Addendum, and IPC 1791 Assembler—as a key differentiator for high-reliability medical and military circuit card assemblies. The company also highlights its in-house engineering team, including electro-mechanical designers, electrical design engineers, and test engineers, as a distinction from typical contract manufacturers.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ITAR','RoHS','IPC 610 Trusted Source Supplier','IPC J-STD-001 Space Addendum','IPC 1791 Trusted Assembler']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "System-Level Assembly (SLA) and integration", "Automated inspection and functional test", "Higher Level Assembly (HLA) / box build", "New Product Introduction (NPI) including first article builds", "Program management with weekly meetings and Gantt charts", "Test development and custom test solutions", "Supply chain services (BOM analysis, obsolescence management, global sourcing)", "AS5553 counterfeit mitigation", "IPC 610 Class 2/3 compliance", "IPC A-7711/21 rework, repair, and modification", "IPC 1791 Trusted Assembler", "IPC J-STD-001 Space Addendum", "GIDEP membership", "Flow-down adherence", "Silicon Expert BOM risk analysis", "Weekly material availability reviews", "Detailed assembly instruction creation", "Production operator training", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Chassis and enclosure integration", "Design for manufacturability support"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["11 SMT lines", "Automated inspection systems"], "volume": "Low to medium volume, high mix", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Comprehensive certifications (AS9100, ISO 13485, ITAR, IPC 610 Trusted Source, IPC J-STD-001 Space Addendum)", "In-house engineering staff (electro-mechanical designers, electrical design engineers, test engineers)", "100% test for every assembly delivered", "AS5553 Counterfeit Mitigation Compliant and GIDEP member since 2015", "Focus on low-to-medium volume, high-complexity, high-reliability assemblies"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Baltimore, MD; Richardson, TX; Bloomington, IL -> /about", "Certifications: AS9100, ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR, RoHS, IPC 610 Trusted Source, IPC J-STD-001 Space Addendum, IPC 1791 Trusted Assembler -> db, /about", "Facility: 180,000 sq ft, 11 SMT lines, 3 sites -> /about", "Market mix: 85% defense/aerospace, 10% medical, 5% commercial/industrial -> /about", "Management team: Matt Turpin (President & CEO), Jason Glass (CFO), Michael Seltzer (CCO), Waleid Jabai (CTO), Clint Fleming (VP GM Baltimore), John Lutostanksi (VP GM Bloomington), Avis Duncan (VP GM Dallas) -> /about", "Capabilities: PCBA, SLA, inspection/test, HLA, NPI, program management, test development, supply chain services -> /capabilities", "Volume: low to medium volume, high complexity/high reliability -> /capabilities", "In-house engineering resources -> /capabilities", "100% test for every assembly -> /capabilities", "AS5553 Counterfeit Mitigation Compliant, GIDEP member since 2015 -> /capabilities", "Mission critical focus: products protect country, infrastructure, warfighter -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Zentech is an Electronic Manufacturing Services (EMS) company with a focus is on the defense, aerospace, and medical industries. We manufacture highly complex, mission critical electronic and electromechanical assemblies", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zentech-manufacturing-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='4 B Plastics Inc operates from Baton Rouge, Louisiana, where it was founded in 1982. The company is led by Steven Braud, who heads a team of master machinists and technicians. Since its start, the business has focused on supplying high-quality PTFE components and custom-machined parts to industrial customers.

The company compression-molds its own unfilled and filled PTFE rod and tube stock, maintaining control from billet to finished part. Its shop custom machines OEM replacement parts — including lantern rings, compressor rings, V-rings, valve repair kits, bushings, bearings, seals, gaskets, and spacers — to customer specifications, often delivering in days. 4 B Plastics also stocks and sells the raw PTFE and specialty thermoplastic materials for customers who machine their own parts.

Primary customers are chemical plants, paper mills, and valve repair shops across the U.S. and abroad. The company supports international projects and corrosion-control systems worldwide, with testimonials citing 24/7 emergency supply during plant turnarounds. Technicians review specs and drawings alongside client project managers to coordinate timely delivery and export logistics.

4 B Plastics differentiates itself with same-day rush capability, in-house PTFE molding for quality assurance, and a master-machinist team that can turn custom orders around in days rather than weeks. Customers highlight competitive pricing and the ability to respond to middle-of-the-night or weekend emergencies that prevent costly downtime.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Compression molding of PTFE", "Custom CNC machining", "OEM replacement part manufacturing", "Valve repair kit assembly", "PTFE rod and tube stocking and sales", "Specialty thermoplastic material supply", "Rush/emergency order fulfillment", "Spec and drawing review", "Export logistics coordination"], "industries": ["Chemical processing", "Pulp and paper", "Valve repair and maintenance", "Corrosion control systems"], "materials": ["PTFE (unfilled)", "PTFE (filled)", "Specialty thermoplastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day turnaround for rush jobs; days for custom machining", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day turnaround on rush orders", "In-house compression molding of PTFE rod and tube for quality control", "Custom machining to spec in days, not weeks", "24/7 emergency supply during plant turnarounds", "Master machinists review specs and drawings for precise fit"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 -> db", "Headquarters Baton Rouge, Louisiana -> db", "Steven Braud leads company -> /", "Compression molds own PTFE rod and tube stock -> /", "Custom machines OEM replacement parts (lantern rings, compressor rings, V-rings, valve repair kits, bushings, bearings, seals, gaskets, spacers) -> /", "Stocks and sells unfilled/filled PTFE and specialty thermoplastics -> /", "Serves chemical plants, paper plants, valve repair shops -> /", "Supports international projects and corrosion control systems worldwide -> /", "Offers 24/7 emergency supply during turnarounds -> /", "Technicians review specs and drawings -> /", "Same-day turnaround for rush jobs -> /", "Master machinists turn custom orders in days -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "WE ALSO MANUFACTURE CUSTOM ORDERS. The Master Machinists at 4B Plastics will custom machine the parts you need to your specifications in just days.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='4-b-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='4G Steel Fabrication operates from Lincoln, Nebraska, in the center of the American heartland. The company was launched in February 2015 by four partners — the “4 Guys” behind the name — and is now owned and operated by two of the original founders, Charlie Fleck and Tim Limon. Their goal was to build the most efficient and productive structural steel fabrication business in the region while creating a workplace where employees could build long-term careers with strong benefits.

The shop specializes in structural and miscellaneous steel fabrication for commercial and institutional projects. Recent work includes the 925-ton Canopy Park in Lincoln, 887 tons for the University of Nebraska’s Mabel Lee Hall, 810 tons for Wichita State University’s Woolsey Hall, 495 tons for SCC Health Sciences, 322 tons for ICM in Colwich, Kansas, and 263 tons for Summerland Schools in Ewing, Nebraska. The company emphasizes the use of current fabrication technologies to maintain quality across projects of varying scale.

Primary customers are in education, healthcare, public infrastructure, and industrial construction. Project owners include public universities, school districts, healthcare systems, and municipal developments across Nebraska and Kansas.

