UPDATE companies SET description='AC Horn Manufacturing traces its roots to a modest garage in Dallas, Texas, where the company was founded in 1907 as a small sheet metal operation. The business took its modern shape in 1946 when A.C. ''Ace'' Horn assumed leadership of his father''s enterprise, establishing a philosophy built on integrity and keeping one''s word.

Today, Horn designs and builds processing equipment for the snack food industry, including popcorn cookers and coaters, continuous and batch nut roasters, peanut blanchers, nut butter mills, corn masa mills for tortillas and chips, and pellet puffing systems. The product line also features the modular M360 platform that allows customers to scale automation as production grows. A job shop division provides custom fabrication services.

Horn serves snack food manufacturers of all sizes, from smaller regional processors to global corporations. Its equipment is used for popcorn, roasted and coated nuts, Japanese-style peanuts, nut butters, corn-based snacks, and puffed pellets. The company''s customer base spans the broader food processing sector, with particular depth in nut and snack applications.

The company attributes its differentiation to a century-old commitment to craftsmanship — using high-quality components, thoughtful design, and no shortcuts — backed by an unrivaled service pledge to fix issues quickly and provide ongoing technical support. The 2024 acquisition by PROBAT, another family-owned firm, was framed as a cultural fit that would strengthen both organizations through vertical integration and shared expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Popcorn cooking and coating", "Continuous nut roasting", "Batch nut roasting", "Peanut blanching (split and whole)", "Japanese peanut coating", "Nut butter milling", "Corn masa milling for tortillas and chips", "Snack pellet puffing", "Batch nut coating", "Custom equipment fabrication (job shop)", "Equipment customization and modular automation integration"], "industries": ["Snack food manufacturing", "Nut processing", "Popcorn production", "Confectionery and coated snacks", "Corn-based snack production", "Food processing equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["M320 Popcorn Cooker/Coater", "Telford Turbo-Flo Continuous Nut Roaster", "Batch Roasters", "M360 Modular Processing Line", "Stoneless Masa Mill"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Equipment built with high-quality components and no-shortcuts design philosophy", "Unrivaled customer service commitment including rapid issue resolution and ongoing technical support", "Modular M360 platform allowing scalable automation upgrades", "In-house job shop for custom fabrication and machine customization"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1907 in Dallas, Texas -> /about-us", "A.C. ''Ace'' Horn took over father''s sheet metal business in 1946 -> /about-us", "Family-owned, Michael Horn president & CEO -> /", "Acquired by PROBAT Group February 2024 -> /", "Approximately 1,000 employees -> db", "Product lines: popcorn, nut roasting, blanching, coating, milling, pellet puffing -> /", "Equipment: M320 Cooker/Co